docs/research/canon-decisions/0047-power-multi-layer-decomposition.md:187:- **Unchanged**: ADR-0005, ADR-0044, ADR-0045, ADR-0046, ADR-0001 files (all relationships narrated in ADR-0047 prose per operator directive).
docs/research/connections/canon-rebuild-arc-method-retrospective.md:33:ADR-0044 reopened the core thesis because the canon's self-description had drifted away from the grammar actually earned by prior corpus work. That opened a harder question than "fix the wording": how do you extend, clarify, decompose, or decline candidate concepts without treating every conceptual pressure as a reason to mint a new primitive?
docs/research/connections/canon-rebuild-arc-method-retrospective.md:99:ADR-0044 aligned the core thesis with the roster that corpus work had already validated rather than the older "five primitives" story. That did two things at once:
docs/research/connections/canon-rebuild-arc-method-retrospective.md:199:- **plan-vs-evidence re-verification**: ADR-0044 and ADR-0049 surfaced that plan summaries can lag the live evidence base
docs/research/connections/canon-rebuild-arc-method-retrospective.md:473:- **core rebuild and post-Phase-3b queue formation**: ADR-0044 through ADR-0055
docs/research/connections/canon-rebuild-arc-method-retrospective.md:478:The quickest ADR entry points for a collaborator such as Jeff are ADR-0044, ADR-0048, ADR-0054, ADR-0065, ADR-0066, ADR-0069, and ADR-0070. Those seven decisions expose most of the method shifts named in `§3` and `§4`, while the surrounding ADRs show the method operating at full resolution.
