docs/research/canon-decisions/0059-downstream-bounded-parkings-cleanup.md:68:**D1 — Self-similarity residual in decision-memo.md**: ADR-0044 deleted the self-similarity / node-as-graph framing. One table row in `docs/synthesis/decision-memo.md:305` still cites "Spore's self-similarity principle (node-as-graph)". Reworded to current scale-nested-holons vocabulary while preserving the functional claim.
docs/research/canon-decisions/0050-sociality-side-b-plus-primitive.md:46:  - spore:ADR-0044-core-thesis-primitive-roster-alignment
docs/research/canon-decisions/0050-sociality-side-b-plus-primitive.md:233:- **IC / PM coordinated-update of their grammars**: deferred per plan Non-goals. IC and PM reference Spore's primitive grammar via ADR-0044 cross-references; the 8→9 move is not auto-propagated. Each project decides independently whether to follow. Post-Phase-3b coordinated-propagation may bundle 3b.4 + 3b.5a together since both are roster-extensions of the ADR-0044 baseline.
docs/research/canon-decisions/0050-sociality-side-b-plus-primitive.md:237:- **Frame-acknowledgment preserved**. ADR-0050's Side-B commitment is scope-conditioned per ADR-0031/0032: Spore's primitive grammar operates at the social-coordination-among-sovereign-agents-capable-of-declaring-intent layer. Alternative coordination frames (autopoiesis, distributed-systems, sub-symbolic) operate at different layers. ADR-0050 does not claim sociality is universally irreducible; it claims Spore canon commits to the irreducibly-joint reading at Spore's scoped layer.
docs/research/canon-decisions/0050-sociality-side-b-plus-primitive.md:281:- **ADR-0044**: 7-primitive-roster-alignment; ADR-0049 extended to 8; ADR-0050 extends to 9.
docs/research/canon-decisions/0050-sociality-side-b-plus-primitive.md:291:- No ADR-0002 / ADR-0016 / ADR-0044 / ADR-0045 / ADR-0046 / ADR-0047 / ADR-0048 / ADR-0049 file modifications (all extended via prose cross-reference only; ADR-0001 unchanged).
docs/research/canon-decisions/0044-core-thesis-primitive-roster-alignment.md:15:  The Core Thesis text in docs/project-vision.md is out-of-sync with Spore's actual canon-blessed primitive roster. The text names a "five primitives" list (sovereign identity / shared memory / commitment protocols / governance patterns / federation rules) that is NOT the primitive roster CFR-v1 (corpus-foundational-review-v1) blessed. The actual roster — traceable through ADR-0008 (field), ADR-0013 (intent/evidence), ADR-0016 (field/holon distinction), ADR-0025 (primitive-roster-boundary-cleanup), and foundations docs — is seven primitives in two kinds: three structural primitives (field, holon, membrane) that describe the substrate of coordination, and four coordination verbs (intent, commitment, evidence, signal) that describe the operations through which agents coordinate. The Phase 1 coherence-and-falsifiability audit flagged C-01 (primitive-list-universality), C-02 (composability-scope overclaim), C-03 (list-count mismatch between 5-primitives / 6-ecology / 8-projections), and C-10 (self-similarity scope-overreach) as coherence defects in the Core Thesis section. This ADR aligns the Core Thesis to the actual canon-blessed roster + closes those four dispositions. Phase 3b (next session) will address the capstone's separately-identified gaps (Care / Norms / Power / Reproduction / Identity).
