docs/project-vision.md:10:Spore is an infrastructure for collective agency — a common grammar for plural, sovereign coordination across scales and scopes. It operates across the normative commitments that shape how agents see, value, know, and act (ontological, axiological, epistemological, practical). It develops and publishes **Agent Commons**: a pattern language, protocol family, and governance-memory pattern that enables coordination and coherence without surrendering sovereignty. Here "agent" means any entity with enough coherence to perceive, decide, and act: a person, an AI, a team, an organization, a federation, a mixed human-AI collective.
docs/project-vision.md:32:    - *Co-presence-mode scope* (ADR-0064; closes ADR-0055 R-Enc-1 via scope-conditioning; Trigger E-5 fired): Spore's Field primitive operationally spans two Field-condition-modes, and the reading that applies depends on the instantiation context — canon commits to both as operationally valid rather than privileging one as universal. **Co-presence-requiring fields** are constituted by common-knowledge-of-mutual-attention among participants: the Field-conditions in which coordination-verbs fire include a shared temporal-spatial (or virtual-co-located) window where each participant attends to the same situation and knows that others are attending (BKC/Octo quarterly federation meetings where attendance-pledge is the irreducibly-joint case per ADR-0055 framing-note §3.2; synchronous governance-artifact authoring sessions where joint-focus determines what can be jointly evaluated; DW design-reviews on calls and pair-programming). This reading aligns with Lewis/Schiffer/Chwe common-knowledge-philosophy (co-presence creates common knowledge), Goffman 1963/1967/1974 and Collins 2004 micro-sociology interaction-order (focused interaction as common focus of cognitive and visual attention; interaction rituals as bounded mutual-focus-of-attention generating solidarity), and Schutz 1967 phenomenological we-relation (vivid present / growing older together). **Co-presence-non-requiring fields** are constituted by asynchronous-capable coordination: the Field-conditions support coordination operations without mutual-attention substrate (Octo autonomous research with stigmergic trace substitution; PM `pm:MatchProposal` progressive-disclosure designed for async message exchange with `pm:TemporalWindow` providing scheduling rather than co-presence; async PR-review governance; async spec-DAG amendment text-authoring per ADR-0041 text-authoritative discipline). This reading aligns with ADR-0041 text-authoritative discipline and stigmergic-coordination-as-substrate. Which mode is load-bearing is evaluated per Field instantiation; mixed dual-mode cases (federation protocol-version negotiation with co-presence-requiring deliberation phase and non-requiring ratification phase; IC memory-governance with individual-async and collective-co-present modes; joint-commitment formation that is structurally co-presence-like but achievable asynchronously via common-knowledge-under-defined-window; spec-DAG amendment with sync deliberation and async text-authoring; DW stand-ups in async text versus design-reviews in sync calls) are canonically legible as combinations rather than residual ambiguity. ADR-0064 declined to admit `co-presence-Field-condition` as Field sub-stratification (ADR-0046-parallel) or property-on-Field — earning-test Q-a marginal (names a Field-condition-mode rather than a new coordination operation), Q-b partial (2 strong co-presence-requiring cases + 2 clear non-requiring counter-cases + 5 dual-mode/ambiguous cases), tradition-breadth 2 full clusters (A common-knowledge-philosophy + B micro-sociology-interaction-order) meets ≥2 scope-conditioning threshold but does not clear ≥3 threshold for heavier admission once Johar-native (F) is not counted as full third cluster on honest-rigor grounds. Scope-conditioning of the existing Field primitive preserves the ADR-0046 rule-level stratification (ORTHOGONAL axis: rule-levels govern coordination-action-type; co-presence-mode governs situational-substrate) and stabilizes the ADR-0055 Encounter framing-note's Lewis/Schiffer reference (line 97) by giving mutual-attention as Field-condition a canonical home at Field-bullet level without reopening Encounter disposition. This is the **third application of the primitive-bullet scope-conditioning pattern** (after ADR-0062 Membrane production-mode and ADR-0063 Signal sense-making-mode) and completes the **autopoiesis-enactive tension canonical resolution triad** across all three structural primitives.
docs/project-vision.md:33:    - See ADR-0008 (collective-agency placement), ADR-0046 (rule-level stratification; ORTHOGONAL axis to co-presence-mode), ADR-0047 (power-axis on rule-setting), ADR-0055 (Encounter framing-note stabilized by co-presence-Field-condition scope-conditioning), ADR-0064 (co-presence-mode scope).
docs/project-vision.md:68:    - *Sense-making-mode scope* (ADR-0063; capstone §8 Tier-3 item 16; closes ADR-0053 R-Sig-1): The Signal primitive operationally spans two sense-making-modes, and canon commits to both as valid rather than privileging one. **Sender-receiver signals** transmit perturbation across a coordination channel: one party encodes, another decodes; meaning is carried by the signal rather than constituted in the exchange (algedonic urgency bypassing hierarchy, stigmergic traces indirectly coordinating through environmental modification, federation protocol-version dissemination, governance-artifact ratification broadcast, spec-DAG event emission). This reading is the operational default and is supported across MARL/VSM/DS/ABM/REA/Trust. **Participatory-sense-making signals** (De Jaegher & Di Paolo 2007) are constitutively interactive: in deliberation-phase and formation-phase coordination (BKC pool-formation deliberation where the scope of a commitment-pool emerges between deliberants; IC memory-governance curation where what gets preserved and attributed is co-enacted in ongoing exchange; joint-commitment formation per ADR-0050 where Gilbert's *form-joint-commitment* operation is irreducibly a joint act constituted by mutual expression under common knowledge), meaning is not transmitted between pre-formed parties but emerges in the interaction process itself, which can acquire operational closure and autonomy per De Jaegher & Di Paolo. Ambiguous dual-phase cases (federation protocol-version *negotiation* before adoption; PM matchmaking dialogue refining `pm:CommitmentBundle` scope before ratification; spec-DAG amendment deliberation before text-authoritative authoring) are canonically legible as combinations — participatory sense-making during the formation/deliberation phase followed by sender-receiver transmission during the dissemination/adoption phase. Which mode is load-bearing depends on the signal instance. ADR-0063 declined to promote `participatory-sense-making` to derived glossary slug, property-on-primitive, or primitive (earning test did not jointly pass: Q-a marginal on protocol surface — De Jaegher/Di Paolo's interaction-process operations of entry/exit, cadence, mutual incorporation, repair are thinly specified at Spore's operational layer; Q-b partial — three supporting cases, three counter-cases, three dual-phase cases; single-tradition-support concern per ADR-0053 R-Sig-1 maintained — adjacent traditions such as Bakhtin/Vygotsky dialogism, Hutchins distributed cognition, Schutz phenomenological we-relations, and Wittgenstein language-games support the family claim *"meaning is intersubjective"* without independently arriving at PSM's specific mechanism) and chose scope-conditioning of the existing primitive instead. The ADR-0053 autopoiesis-objection acknowledgment above is unchanged; ADR-0063 adds the positive-articulation scope that ADR-0053 §R-Sig-1 parked for dedicated evaluation. Side-B-relationship note: PSM is the *enactive* form of Side-B (meaning constitutively interactive); ADR-0050's `joint-commitment` primitive is the *Gilbertian* form (obligation constitutively joint). Per ADR-0050 line 141, PSM remains accessible as "mode-of-joint-commitment-operation" — the enactive characterization of how joint-commitment-formation proceeds; admitted `joint-commitment` and cited-lineage PSM are **parallel Side-B articulations**, not competing or sequential primitives.
docs/project-vision.md:85:This commitment is *scoped*, not universal. Spore's primitive grammar operates at the social-coordination-among-sovereign-agents-capable-of-declaring-intent layer (per scope-conditioning ADR-0031/0032); alternative frames (autopoiesis sub-symbolic coupling; distributed-systems message-passing; pluriversal kinship-ontology held under ADR-0001) operate at other layers and may answer the reducibility question differently.
docs/project-vision.md:130:**Scope of composability.** Across Spore's three operational instance families (BKC/Octo, Poietic Match, personal-operator), the nine primitives appear as recognisable structures and operations at each scale Spore has reached, with scale-appropriate differences in formalization, party composition, and governance conditions. Whether this composability extends to arbitrary coordination systems at arbitrary scales is a research question, not a demonstrated property.
docs/project-vision.md:201:**Scale instantiation.** Each coordination verb is realized at every scale Spore has reached. Coordination enters when multiple agents' loops overlap and need to interoperate across holon membranes and field substrate. Economic coordination under discovery cannot rely on wage or transaction grammar because those forms depend on specifiability, containment, and measurability assumptions that discovery structurally violates; under such conditions, governance structure rather than contract terms becomes the necessary basis for coordination. Participation in commitment-based coordination requires standing — security, capability, and membership conditions without which formal participation rights are structurally empty.
