tmp/sheaf-explorer-design-workflow-output-2026-05-30.json:112:      "attribution_in_ui": "FIVE attribution surfaces (load-bearing — sheaf-explorer's LLM-context bundle auto-ingests this content into public/llms-full.txt per audit material_finding #8, so attribution discipline is read by both on-page humans AND downstream LLMs):\n\n1. ROLE-CHIP HOVER TOOLTIP: each of the 7 chips, on hover, shows \"<role-name> · Per Sahely 2026 C-11 (From Entanglement to Governance, Ch 3 pp37-44). One of three labelings of these 7 points in this lab.\"\n\n2. LENS-TOGGLE SUBHEAD: directly under the 3-pill segmented control, fixed sub-text reads: \"Each lens is a different labeling of the same 7 Fano-plane points. Sahely's labeling is HIS interpretation; canonical PG(2,2) is the abstract structure; the operator-7-primitive lens is an illustrative sketch (Spore did NOT canonize a Fano-grammar — see §3.1 of the bridge note).\"\n\n3. INVARIANT-MODE EXPLAINER: when 'Show invariant triads' fires, the explanatory sentence is exactly: \"The 7 channels are properties of the Fano-plane structure, not of any particular labeling. Sahely's contribution is INTERPRETING these 7 invariant lines as 7 functional channels of any coordination system. Whether to ACCEPT that interpretation is open — see §3.1 + §3.2 of the bridge note for cluster-counting + closure-uniqueness-earning-test considerations.\" This sentence does the load-bearing work of preventing the UI from implying canonical-status for Sahely's reading.\n\n4. DEEP-MATH PANEL (under '▾ Go deeper'): three paragraphs each ending with citation. Para 1 cites PG(2,2) (1892, no Sahely attribution — this is canonical). Para 2 cites Steiner triple systems (S(2,3,7) uniqueness — also canonical). Para 3 is THE Sahely paragraph and reads: \"Sahely's argument (per Ch 3, pp37-44 of *From Entanglement to Governance*) is that pairwise relations cannot achieve closure, triadic closure suffices and is minimal, and the Fano plane is therefore the unique finite structure satisfying triadic closure — from which 7 functional channels follow. Spore canon has NOT adopted closure-uniqueness as a primitive-admission earning-test (Spore admitted joint-commitment via cross-tradition convergence — ADR-0050, ADR-0048 — not Fano-derivation). This lab presents Sahely's interpretation as ONE labeling among several; readers should consult the bridge note for the comparative analysis.\"\n\n5. ATTRIBUTION FOOTER (always-visible at component bottom, 11px #64748b):\n   \"Sahely 7-role labeling and channel-names per B. Sahely, *From Entanglement to Governance: The Geometry of Coherence Across Scales* (2026-04-02), Ch 3 pp 37-44 + C-11 pp 39-40. Spore bridge note: [spore.connection.sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis §3.2](github.com/DarrenZal/spore/.../sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md). Sahely's framing is HIS, not sheaf.lol-original. This lab is pedagogical articulation under CC BY-SA 4.0 (see sheaf.lol/LICENSE-CONTENT).\"\n\nWHAT THE UI DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO:\n- Does NOT show 'Sahely' as the default/canonical label on the chips (chips show role-letters + role-names; Sahely-attribution is on the chip ONLY via hover-tooltip, and the lens-toggle gives equal visual weight to all 3 labelings).\n- Does NOT auto-select 'Sahely' lens on mount — initial state is unfilled, user chooses.\n- Does NOT show Sahely's channel-names (Geometry-of-viability etc.) under non-Sahely lenses (numerical lens shows only numerals; operator-sketch lens shows only primitive-names + 'no Sahely-canonical name' for unmatched triples).\n- Does NOT call Sahely's reading 'the' grammar or 'the' rubric anywhere in body text — uses 'Sahely's grammar' / 'Sahely's rubric' consistently.\n- Does NOT imply Spore endorses the closure-uniqueness earning-test — the Deep-Math panel explicitly notes Spore's NON-adoption.\n\nINVARIANT EXPLANATION (load-bearing): the lab's centerpiece pedagogical move is showing that the LINE STRUCTURE is invariant under re-labeling, while the ROLE INTERPRETATION is not. This is the only structurally honest way to teach \"Sahely's framework\" without endorsing it: present Sahely as ONE labeling that gives the 7 lines a particular meaning, and let the reader hold that interpretation up against the canonical structure + the operator-sketch.",
tmp/sheaf-explorer-design-workflow-output-2026-05-30.json:122:        "ATTRIBUTION AMBIGUITY IN INTERACTIVE UI: a reader who lands directly on §10i without reading the intro paragraph may interact with the lens-toggle, see 'Sahely 2026' as the default-selected lens (if implementation sets it as default), and form the belief 'sheaf.lol endorses Sahely's grammar as canonical.' Mitigation set: (i) initial state has NO lens auto-selected — chips start empty, user must drag or click a preset; (ii) all three preset buttons (Sahely / canonical / operator-sketch) sit in equal-weight pills; (iii) the load-bearing 'invariance + interpretation' sentence (per attribution_in_ui #3) fires the moment user toggles 'Show invariant triads' which is the natural first interaction after placing 7 chips; (iv) always-visible attribution footer carries Spore's NON-adoption posture explicitly.",
