tmp/sahely-phase-3-handoff-2026-05-30.md:113:3. **3-layer separation discipline** (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`) — Phase 3 is bridge-note authoring (Layer 1); any canon-pressure surfaced flows to a DECISION-BRIEF (Layer 2) at `tmp/`; any admission requires dedicated ADR (Layer 3). Layer-distinctness is load-bearing.
tmp/jeff-shawn-spore-next-steps-2026-04-13.md:11:Spore / Agent Commons looks increasingly like the grammar layer: claims, evidence, attestation, holons, intents, commitments, governance DAGs, federation. Not a platform in the usual sense, but something more upstream: a coordination grammar that shapes what kinds of applications and institutions are thinkable and buildable without requiring centralization.
tmp/jeff-shawn-spore-next-steps-2026-04-13.md:23:- Spore / Agent Commons: coordination grammar
tmp/canon-coherence-falsifiability-handoff-prompt.md:18:Spore is a project developing a coordination grammar ("Agent Commons") for plural, sovereign coordination across scales. It has been in development ~2 years. The canon has been through four canon-review rounds (R1-R4) producing 40 ADRs, plus an adversarial-critique cycle and two prior first-principles audits (v1 and v2). R1-R4 surfaced within-frame refinements. v2 (produced by integrating 4 parallel lens agents + 2 independent second-opinions from Codex and Claude Opus 4.7) surfaced frame-level issues the within-frame work could not reach.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-codex-2026-04-22.md:36:- the six-element ecology as if it were the default anatomy of coordination rather than one coordination grammar ([docs/project-vision.md:72-89](../docs/project-vision.md), [docs/foundations/constitutional-artifacts-and-graph-projections.md:28-41](../docs/foundations/constitutional-artifacts-and-graph-projections.md))
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-codex-2026-04-22.md:91:More earned than several other borrowings because there is actual implementation-adjacent evidence in commitment pooling, Celo settlement, and BKC routing ([docs/project-vision.md:201-203](../docs/project-vision.md), [docs/patterns/commitment-pooling.md:81-85](../docs/patterns/commitment-pooling.md)). This is still not proof that the whole coordination grammar reduces to commitment economy, but it is not decorative borrowing.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-codex-2026-04-22.md:97:**Verdict:** keep, but demote from universal skeleton to a scoped coordination grammar.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-codex-2026-04-22.md:103:I would not delete the ecology. I would relabel it as **Spore's discovery-mode coordination grammar**, then separately say that maintenance-mode, ritual, conversational, stigmergic, and embedded-care coordination can compress or bypass parts of it.
docs/foundations/spore-instance-model.md:15:How the coordination grammar materializes in running systems — without prescribing a single implementation path.
docs/foundations/spore-instance-model.md:67:1. **Grammar use** — the holon performs at least one Spore coordination-grammar operation (intent, commitment, joint-commitment, evidence, signal, reproduction; or governance-artifact authoring under spec-DAG discipline) in a canon-legible way through one or more of Canon, Node, Agent, or Site.
