tmp/sahely-foundation-payloads/req-20180306-eco-genocidal-system.json:1:{"name": "Sahely 2018-03-06 Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen (foundation-era)", "content": "A 2018 foundation-era Sahely-original essay arguing that financial sanctions and austerity constitute *structural* weapons of mass destruction while ideological mass-media filtering constitutes *cultural* weapons of mass destruction (deception), both serving \"the multiplying money-cancer class\" that deprives people of universal human life necessities. Sahely connects Galtung's structural/cultural violence framework (via Paul E. Farmer 2006) to John McMurtry's civil-commons and cancer-stage-of-capitalism analyses, proposing that we must structurally institutionalize the provisioning of life-requirements and bring the background weapons of mass deception into full view to end \"the reversal of humanity's social evolution.\" Epistemic status: foundation-era (pre-AI-collaboration, ai_co_authored:false), single-curator selection from one Sahely-corpus author; recurrence across the corpus is not independent evidence. Sahely-authored original (is_repost:false) that embeds verbatim primary-source quotes from Galtung/Farmer and McMurtry, attributed via citation.", "source_description": "Sahely foundation-era post (2017-2018, pre-AI), bsahely.com", "source_document": "https://bsahely.com/2018/03/06/eco-genocidal-system-violence-still-unseen-structural-and-cultural-weapons-of-mass-destruction-by-the-multiplying-money-cancer-class/", "facts": [{"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "AUTHORED_BY", "object": "Bichara Sahely", "fact_text": "The 2018 foundation-era essay 'Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen' is a Sahely-original work (is_repost:false), authored by Bichara Sahely.", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object": "structural violence", "fact_text": "Sahely's connective argument claims that financial sanctions and austerity are structural weapons of mass destruction, destroying lives en masse by depriving people of access to universal human life necessities like food, water, healthcare, and education (C-4).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object": "money-value", "fact_text": "Sahely claims the IMF, World Bank, BIS and WTO construct rules that incapacitate countries and bind them to unpayable debt owed to private transnational banking money-sequencing cartels, making these institutions culprits of structural weapons of mass destruction (C-5).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object": "cultural violence", "fact_text": "Sahely claims ideologies like neoliberalism and religious fundamentalism use cultural weapons of mass destruction, filtering mass media to prop up the system and conceal hidden eco-genocidal structural machinations (C-6).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "INTRODUCES", "object": "life-value", "fact_text": "Sahely enumerates six categories of universal human life necessities (clean air/water/soils; nourishing food; shelter; social inclusion/safety/healthcare; education/recreation/meaningful work; social justice) that must be provided for all humanity via collective mass life-regeneration (C-7).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "ENGAGES_CONCEPT", "object": "civil commons", "fact_text": "Sahely defines the civil commons as 'any and all social constructs which enable universal access to human life goods without which people's capacities are always reduced' (C-8).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "DISTINGUISHES", "object": "structural violence", "fact_text": "The essay distinguishes structural weapons of mass destruction (financial: sanctions, austerity via IMF/World Bank/BIS/WTO) from cultural weapons of mass destruction (ideological: neoliberalism/fundamentalism plus mass-media filtering), framing both as serving the money-cancer class (C-4, C-5, C-6).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "CITES_AUTHOR", "object": "Johan Galtung", "fact_text": "The essay cites Johan Galtung for the definitions of structural violence (via Paul E. Farmer 2006 'Box 1') and cultural violence (Galtung, 'Cultural Violence'), quoted as epigraphs (C-1, C-2, C-3).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "CITES_AUTHOR", "object": "John McMurtry", "fact_text": "The essay embeds verbatim quotes from John McMurtry's 'Corporate Globalization versus The Civil Commons' (civil-commons layers, apical money-sequencers, reversal of social evolution) and 'The Cancer Stage of Capitalism' (no discipline grounded in life requirements) (C-9, C-10, C-13).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "ENGAGES_CONCEPT", "object": "civil commons", "fact_text": "Quoting McMurtry, the essay frames the civil commons as the lost common ground of our lives and the substance of social justice not yet recognised in received theory and doctrine, now under attack by defunding, deregulation, and for-profit privatization (C-9, C-10).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object": "life-coherence", "fact_text": "Quoting McMurtry's 'The Cancer Stage of Capitalism', the essay claims no established school or theory has grounded itself in life requirements; instead some social construct (the state, the market, a class, technology) is invariably adopted as the ultimate reference rather than the life-ground itself (C-13).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "REFRAMES", "object": "life-value", "fact_text": "Sahely's closing argues we must structurally institutionalize the provisioning of life-requirements and culturally internalize the necessity of securing the social and planetary life-grounds, while bringing the background weapons of mass deception into full view to end 'the reversal of humanity's social evolution' (C-11, C-12).", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}, {"subject": "Eco-Genocidal System Violence Still Unseen", "predicate": "IN_CLUSTER_WITH", "object": "TOWARDS LIFE-KNOWLEDGE", "fact_text": "This essay is the earliest foundation-era anchor (Phase 3, 2017\u20132018 pre-Gmail tranche) seeding the structural+cultural violence \u2194 civil-commons / money-cancer-class theme that later 2026 AI-co-authored Grammar of Violence and Global Projections (Galtung) notes elaborate.", "valid_from": "2018-03-06"}], "group_id": "personal", "create_entities": true}
