docs/research/connections/sahely-maturana-viability-grammar.md:42:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-21 white paper *"Toward a Maturana-Informed Viability Grammar: Deriving Diagnostic Distinctions from Living, Love, Conversation, and Culture"* (172 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely per §1 below). It is a **descriptive** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the 3-layer intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`): bridge note surfaces canon-pressure CANDIDATES; honest-rigor cluster-counting and ADMIT/DECLINE verdicts belong in the Layer 2 DECISION-BRIEF (`tmp/sahely-corpus-canon-pressure-decision-brief-2026-05-22.md`, authored separately by orchestrator). Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`) — it makes no recommendation for write-side action at IC/bregion/BKC/PM.
