docs/research/connections/sahely-life-value-onto-axiology-civil-commons.md:31:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side **framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact (Layer 1.5 of the 3-layer intake-to-vocab-admission program, `feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`) for the bsahely.com post of 2026-02-22 — a curated republication of a John McMurtry essay collection. It is **descriptive**: it maps the post's themes onto Spore canon that is **already resolved** through the Sahely-corpus Bundle α arc (ADRs 0085–0090; concepts-yaml v24; four cross-cutting doctrines; canon-rebuild arc at 40 canon-decisions). It surfaces **no new canon-pressure** and proposes **no admission**. The Bundle α DECISION-BRIEF work has already run honest-rigor cluster-counting and admitted `life-value-doctrine` (ADR-0086) and `civil-commons` (ADR-0087); this note simply records that this McMurtry-primary source is one of the substrate texts those admissions cite, read against the resolved-state canon. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation. Single-source rigor: this is one author corpus (McMurtry-primary), and cross-post recurrence inside the Sahely corpus is **not independent evidence** — the cluster-counting that earned admission already lives in the Bundle α ADRs, not here.
