docs/research/connections/sahely-reclaiming-our-future.md:33:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-02-24 post *"Reclaiming Our Future: Transforming our Cancer Economy"* — a NotebookLM/ChatGPT-5.2 curated-abstract of John McMurtry's *The Cancer Stage of Capitalism: From Crisis to Cure* (1999/2014). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). Per Phase 3 discipline this note **admits nothing**: it maps post themes onto the **already-resolved** Bundle α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and surfaces no new canon-pressure. Single-source rigor governs throughout: Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus and this post is itself an abstract of a single substrate author (McMurtry) — cross-post recurrence within the Sahely corpus is **not** independent evidence, and this post's claims are McMurtry's, not independent corroboration of Spore's already-admitted McMurtry-substrate canon. The §5 cross-repo delta is descriptive only; it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/connections/sahely-reclaiming-our-future.md:54:This is a Phase-3 lighter-ceremony bridge note. Per the extraction record's cluster role, this abstract is a **Wave-7 same-day-triad member** with the Civil Commons abstract (#4) and the Grammar of Violence anchor (#6), and serves as *"the substrate-explanation for the cancer-analogy anchor #6 uses."* It is the McMurtry economic-substrate explainer for the cancer-economy theme that several Sahely papers invoke; Spore canon has already metabolized that substrate at Bundle α.
docs/research/connections/bioregional-coordination-as-peer-instance-family.md:45:This is **comparative intake, light**. The note registers + cross-cites; it does not merge the bounded contexts. bioregional-coordination retains its bounded context (canon-bearing structure for agentic bioregionalism); Spore retains its bounded context (coordination grammar canon).
docs/research/connections/bioregional-coordination-as-peer-instance-family.md:53:2. **BKC relationship**: **peer at instance-family layer**. Neither downstream of the other. Both compose with Spore coordination grammar at the upstream-reference layer. Cross-citation is at peer level; neither subsumes the other. BKC retains its existing identity as the bioregional-knowledge-commoning aspect; bioregional-coordination broadens scope to include economics, mapping, governance, ecological monitoring, intergenerational stewardship, and other bioregional aspects.
docs/research/connections/sahely-medicine-of-living-coherence.md:52:# Sahely (2026-05-03) Toward a Medicine of Living Coherence ↔ Spore Substrate-Grammar Map (Clinical-Medicine Scale; C10 5th-Cluster Probe)
docs/research/connections/sahely-medicine-of-living-coherence.md:54:**Caveat (read first):** This is the Spore-side substrate-grammar map for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-03 paper *"Toward a Medicine of Living Coherence: A Maturana-Informed Framework for Clinical Care, Public Health, and Health Policy"* (151pp; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). This is **Wave 4 anchor #12, the FINAL substrate-gathering anchor of Phase 2**, calibrated per operator dispatch to probe whether the clinical-medicine paper's 7-pattern grammar and associated substrate elevates C10 R-Health-as-coherent-transition cluster-counting from the Wave-3 #9 4-cluster count (Sahely-Maturana / Salutogenesis / Allostasis-upgraded / Naviaux) toward a 5-cluster count (e.g., Engel biopsychosocial / Barabasi network-medicine / clinical-systems-biology / patient-centered-care). The DECISION-BRIEF (`tmp/sahely-corpus-canon-pressure-decision-brief-2026-05-22.md`) has been operator-ratified with Bundle β + per-candidate dispositions; this bridge note's R-claims therefore carry framing-note-only dispositions that **deepen** ratified substrate, plus an explicit C10 5th-cluster probe-finding (operator-elective DECISION-BRIEF refinement consideration only; no self-ratification). Per the 3-layer separation discipline (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`), this is Layer 1.5 substrate-deepening; no canon-body edits; no commits from this artifact alone.
docs/research/connections/sahely-medicine-of-living-coherence.md:127:  > "11. Disease as Stabilized Loss of Living Coherence; 12. Health as Recoverable Life-Capacity; 13. The Clinical Use of the Seven-Pattern Grammar."
docs/research/connections/sahely-knowledge-not-life-coherent.md:32:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side **descriptive** comparative-intake artifact (Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program; `feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`) for a **foundation-era (2018-09-08)** Bichara Sahely blog post that **reposts** a short John McMurtry life-coherence-of-knowledge text. It is **framing-note-only**: it surfaces no admission proposal, runs no cluster-counting verdict, and recommends no write-side action. **FOUNDATION-ERA framing:** this is a 2017–2018 post, **pre the Dec-2022+ AI-co-authored white-paper explosion** — `ai_co_authored: false`, no LLM-dialogical scaffolding, a curated repost rather than a Sahely-authored synthesis. The Bundle α admission arc (ADR-0085 → ADR-0090, concepts-yaml v24, 4 cross-cutting doctrines, 40 canon-decisions) has already resolved the canon-pressure this McMurtry-life-value cluster generated; this Phase 3 note cites that **resolved** state rather than re-opening it. **Single-source rigor:** Sahely is one author corpus, and this particular post is a *repost* of one McMurtry text — cross-post recurrence within his own curated corpus is **not** independent evidence and is **not** treated as convergence. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`).
docs/research/connections/sahely-clinical-assessment.md:41:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Dr. Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-28 white paper *"The Life-Coherence Clinical Assessment: A Method for Reading Disease as Loss of Life-Capacity"* (41-page PDF; bsahely.com blog post; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It is a Phase-3 broader-cluster bridge note: lighter ceremony than the Phase-2 anchors, and it **admits nothing**. The relevant canon-pressure this paper engages — life-value doctrine, margin-as-reserve, care-cluster scope-conditioning, the trap-shape vocabulary, and perception-as-power — was already dispositioned by the Sahely Bundle α arc (ADR-0085 → ADR-0090, landed 2026-05-23 → 05-29). This note cites the **resolved** canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions) and surfaces no new admission.
docs/research/connections/johar-priceability.md:22:A long essay (5254w) arguing that the refusal to price non-market values does not protect them — it renders them invisible to the coordination systems that determine their survival. The essay proposes priceability as a systemic capacity: the ability of systems to perceive and express interdependent value across temporal, spatial, and relational dimensions. Price is reconstructed from a scalar extraction signal into a living, multi-vector coordination grammar. The argument moves from epistemic critique (single-system valuation produces blindness) through structural proposal (plural exchange modalities, systemic sensing infrastructure) to a redefinition of economy: from optimisation toward composition, from prediction toward learning, from transaction toward relational maintenance.
docs/research/connections/johar-priceability.md:40:### 2. Price as Grammar, Not Signal
docs/research/connections/johar-priceability.md:56:Price should be reconstructed from a unidimensional equivalence signal into a multi-vector coordination grammar that translates between incommensurable value forms without reducing them to sameness. This requires three infrastructural capacities: systemic sensing (relational ledgers for non-financial value), plural valuation protocols (conversion without reduction), and negotiated allocation (contribution as process, not event).
docs/research/connections/johar-priceability.md:61:- **R1**: The Spore lexicon should carry "priceability" as a named design concept: the capacity of a system to perceive and express its interdependent forms of value across temporal, spatial, and relational dimensions. The entry should include: (a) the asymmetry between refusing to price (invisibility) and pricing narrowly (blindness), (b) price as multi-vector coordination grammar rather than scalar equivalence signal, (c) the three infrastructural capacities (systemic sensing, plural valuation, negotiated allocation), and (d) the connection to Spore's existing compositional grammar — priceability is to economic coordination what multi-projection is to knowledge coordination. [target: spore.lexicon] [concept: priceability-and-system-world] TODO: slug-deferred
docs/research/concepts-p2p-wiki.yaml:1012:    one_line_definition: Power axis on Field's 3-level rule-stratification — the capacity to set, amend, and enforce rules at operational / collective-choice / constitutional levels, distributed across participants, roles, and positions. Realizes enumerated-powers-by-role (Debian §4/§5/§6; PEP 13) and polycentric-governance (V. Ostrom 1972; Aligica-Tarko 2012) at primitive-asymmetry level. Layer 1 of ADR-0047's three-layer Power decomposition; built atop ADR-0046.
docs/research/connections/sahely-coherence-to-viability.md:177:- **ω → N3 → I4 three-level invariant hierarchy** (C-3 + C-10): mathematically-grounded three-level architecture of coherence (pairwise / triadic / global). Per extraction §"Composition signals" #1: *"Spore has nothing structurally equivalent — closest is the sensor-actuator-failure-actor-governance F1/F5/F6/F3 cluster but those are domain-doctrines not mathematical invariants. Spore has decided (per ADRs 0049/0050/0067 cluster-counting) that operational coordination grammar does NOT need this level of mathematical formalism."* Composes with **W1.5 R-E7-viability-scalar `decline-with-trigger`** (DECISION-BRIEF carry-forward D2 decline): same family of mathematical-invariant-as-coherence-metric framing; same future-state-with-triggers parking discipline. The ω → N3 → I4 hierarchy is more elaborate than W1.5's quartic-invariant-alone framing but the canon-disposition implication is identical.
docs/research/connections/sahely-coherence-to-viability.md:252:**R-ω-N3-I4-hierarchy** → `framing-note-only`. C-3 + C-8 + C-10 + C-12 articulate three-level invariant hierarchy at mathematical-formalism layer. Per extraction §"Composition signals" #1: Spore has nothing structurally equivalent and has decided (per ADRs 0049/0050/0067 cluster-counting) that operational coordination grammar does NOT need this level of mathematical formalism. Composes with W1.5 R-E7-viability-scalar `decline-with-trigger D2` carry-forward decline (same family: viability-as-mathematical-invariant). No new canon-pressure; composing-with-existing-decline-discipline; framing-note-only.
docs/research/connections/bkc-seven-layer-stack-as-instance-instantiation.md:43:### §2.1 Layer 1: Mapping Workshop
docs/research/connections/bkc-seven-layer-stack-as-instance-instantiation.md:115:The clean mappings are Layer 1 as a composed coordination episode, Layer 3 as commitment pooling, Layer 5 as the Agent aspect of the instance model, and Layer 6 as federation plus federated knowledge exchange.
docs/research/connections/bkc-seven-layer-stack-as-instance-instantiation.md:125:BKC frontmatter and project positioning already cite Spore as upstream coordination grammar. `spore.connection.bkc-as-instance-family` closed one reverse citation by registering BKC as a federation-encounter instance-family. This note closes a different asymmetry: the seven-layer stack itself now has a Spore-side bridge note.
docs/research/connections/protocol-society.md:87:Spore's grammar should explicitly state which stance it is adopting — or clarify that it composes with elements of both without collapsing the distinction. The note's working thesis: Spore sits closer to Bauwens's cosmo-local / open-value-network framing than to Borders's proprietarian framing, because Spore's coordination grammar centers community and field agency rather than individual property rights as the primitive unit. Leaving the stance ambiguous under "protocol society" language risks reading-in of either position by downstream audiences, which is a governance failure mode in its own right.
docs/research/connections/protocol-society.md:140:Max Song's "protocol sovereignty" framing (blockchain networks as self-governing systems analogous to Westphalian nation-states, with territorial integrity, self-governance, non-interference, recognition/legitimacy, and cultural identity as characteristics) is a sibling concept to protocol-society but distinct from Spore's positioning: Spore's coordination grammar is not Westphalian-sovereignty-modeled and does not require full non-interference, so the two framings should not be conflated in external language.
docs/research/planning/corroboration-review-checkpoint-1.md:183:Holding-complexity is the most corpus-central family — every other complexity family and most infrastructure/governance families presuppose it. It names the grammar's raison d'etre: why Spore exists as a coordination grammar at all. Leaving it uncorroborated while reviewing the other four for promotion would create an asymmetry: the design justification would remain unvalidated even as the design components are confirmed.
docs/research/connections/sahely-poetics-of-life-coherence.md:41:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-30 white paper *"The Poetics of Life-Coherence: Beauty, Ritual, Grief, and the Tempo of Living Worlds"* (68 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely per §1 below). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It admits nothing and proposes no canon change. Every resonance below maps to **already-resolved** Bundle-α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) — it cites the resolved ADRs, not any pending DECISION-BRIEF framing. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation for IC/bregion/BKC/PM.
docs/research/connections/sahely-poetics-of-life-coherence.md:55:- **Position in corpus:** this paper is the **poetic-transmission** companion to the 2026-05-21 *Maturana-Informed Viability Grammar* anchor (see `spore.connection.sahely-maturana-viability-grammar`). It extends the same Life-Coherence framework downward into aesthetic/ritual/grief/temporal/commons forms. Same author, same program — not an independent corroboration.
docs/research/connections/hyperstition.md:31:A bridge note on the concept of hyperstition and its structural relationship to Spore's coordination grammar.
docs/research/connections/hyperstition.md:47:Spore's coordination grammar can be read as infrastructure for composing hyperstitions — with structural safeguards that the hyperstition frame alone does not provide.
docs/research/connections/hyperstition.md:60:- Spore is not "a hyperstition framework" — it is a coordination grammar with structural parallels to hyperstition dynamics
docs/research/connections/hyperstition.md:68:Spore's coordination grammar can be read as infrastructure for composing hyperstitions with structural safeguards — it adds accountability, contestability, and evidence requirements that hyperstition theory alone does not provide.
docs/research/connections/johar-fork-in-the-system.md:71:- **R1**: Spore's project vision should name holding-complexity-beyond-control as a design context for the coordination grammar: the structural account of why the grammar's adaptive mechanisms exist and what civilisational condition they respond to. The entry should include: (a) the double mismatch — representational inadequacy of distributed control + tightening energetic surplus — as the structural condition that makes the third path necessary, (b) the two default attractors — authoritarian compression and chaos — as the pathways Spore's design must avoid, (c) complexity-handling capacity as the core design variable — the grammar is complexity-handling infrastructure, not merely a governance improvement, (d) the connection to existing grammar — adaptive coordination (coordination loop), scaffolded relationality (commitment protocols, holon architecture), interdependent sovereignty (overlapping membership, forkability), anti-fragility through learning (learning membrane, attestation decay), and (e) the thermodynamic implication — the grammar must operate under tighter resource constraints than the distributed control paradigm it succeeds. [target: spore.project-vision] [concept: holding-complexity-beyond-control] TODO: slug-deferred
docs/research/connections/sahely-neuropsychiatric-disease.md:86:- **C-8** [anchor: §Figure 3 Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar · orn:source:bsahely-2026-05-27-living-coherence-and-neuropsychiatric-di · pdf-p16] The clinical grammar's **Margin** primitive: clinical question "What reserve remains?"; repair direction (grammar table, pdf-p17): "Restore safety, sleep, nourishment, pacing, support, medication when indicated."
docs/research/connections/sahely-neuropsychiatric-disease.md:88:- **C-9** [anchor: §Figure 3 Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar · orn:source:bsahely-2026-05-27-living-coherence-and-neuropsychiatric-di · pdf-p16] The clinical grammar's **Perception** primitive: clinical question "What is salient?"; repair direction (grammar table, pdf-p17): "Recalibrate salience through safety, testing, dialogue, embodiment, and reality contact."
docs/research/connections/sahely-neuropsychiatric-disease.md:142:The paper's Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar (Constraint / Margin / State / Disturbance / Perception / Regulation / Options) is a **diagnostic rubric** — questions a clinician poses to locate where living coherence has broken down (C-12 process-logic-over-box-stacking). Per the extraction record's own cross-corpus note, it is a clinical specialization of the same author's general 8-primitive viability-grammar (shared: Constraint, Margin, Disturbance, Regulation; specialized: State / Perception / Options). Spore's 9 primitives are **operational coordination acts and structures**, not reflective questions. As in the Phase-2 anchor (`sahely-maturana-viability-grammar.md` §4.1), these grammars occupy adjacent-but-cross-layer canon-object classes: Sahely's clinical grammar is closest in Spore terms to a diagnostic-rubric pattern (M4 design-criteria-pattern / catalog-pattern shape per ADR-0065), not a primitive roster. No primitive-roster pressure.
docs/research/connections/sahely-neuropsychiatric-disease.md:169:Sahely's 2026-05-27 paper derives neuropsychiatric disease from disturbances in living coherence across five layers (autopoiesis / structural coupling / emotioning / felt interiority / emotional sentience) and offers a Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar as a transdiagnostic formulation method. Read against Spore's post-Bundle-α canon, **every resonance maps to already-resolved canon**:
docs/research/connections/platform-cooperativism-constructive.md:97:The constructive proposal is not that Spore *becomes* a platform co-op — Spore is a coordination grammar, not a platform operator. The proposal is that Spore's governance-layer canon can import the platform-cooperativism / open-cooperativism vocabulary as the named external lineage for how Spore-hosting organizations SHOULD be structured when they operate instances for multi-party participation, and as the named discipline for how federation-agreements must carry ownership-structure clauses (not just interoperability clauses). This is a clarify-existing-term disposition: add external lineage, import four-criteria discipline, import scale-drift mitigation from the paired opposition.
docs/research/connections/sahely-when-power-outruns-law.md:31:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-01-04 essay *"When Power Outruns Law: Venezuela, the Caribbean, and the Future of a Rules-Based World"* (37 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.2 + NotebookLM, substantive authorship retained by Sahely). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It surfaces resonances against the **resolved** post-Bundle-α Spore canon (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090); it does **not** propose any admission. Sahely is a single AI-co-authored author corpus — cross-post recurrence within his corpus is **not** independent evidence and is not treated as convergence. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/connections/promise-foundation-commitment-protocol.md:59:The ecosystem maps across nearly the full Spore coordination grammar:
docs/research/connections/sahely-education-biological-matrix.md:39:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for a 2018-01-13 blog post on `bsahely.com` that **reposts** Humberto Maturana & Ximena Paz Dávila's 2006 essay *"Education as viewed from the biological matrix of human existence"* (PRELAC Journal / UNESCO). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It is authored **after** the Sahely Bundle α canon arc closed (2026-05-29; ADRs 0085→0090; concepts-yaml v24; four cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions), so it cites the **resolved** canon state, not a pending DECISION-BRIEF. **It admits nothing.** Where this post's themes touch Spore canon, the relevant canon-pressure was already dispositioned in Bundle α; this note maps the resonances descriptively and surfaces no new admission. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`).
docs/research/synthesis/doubt-plural-selfhood-and-relational-maturity.md:20:A synthesis note on the doubt-plural-selfhood-and-relational-maturity concept, drawn from the Johar human-development intake (Batches 1–2). This is the thinnest human-development family (3 pre-synthesis sources) but conceptually sharp: doubt is not epistemic weakness or indecision but a developmental posture that allows plural selfhood to remain in relation without premature closure. The self is not singular or final; maturity includes learning to inhabit many-ness without fragmentation or domination. Relational maturity means sustaining contact across inner multiplicity and outer complexity — the inner developmental condition for inhabiting Spore's coordination grammar.
docs/research/synthesis/doubt-plural-selfhood-and-relational-maturity.md:114:**Primary: candidate primitive** — Doubt, plural selfhood, and relational maturity name the inner developmental conditions for inhabiting Spore's coordination grammar. Three sources converge on the claim that doubt is generative (not weakness), selfhood is plural (not singular), and maturity means sustaining contact across complexity without collapse into certainty or fragmentation. The concept enriches the grammar's epistemic infrastructure (the learning membrane) with the human-developmental vocabulary for why agents must hold ambiguity — and what happens when the capacity to do so is structurally degraded.
docs/research/planning/holding-complexity-beyond-control-corroboration-pass-1.md:240:**I. Material / energetic constraint.** The thermodynamic foundation is directly corroborated from three independent traditions: Tainter (diminishing marginal returns on complexity investment), Georgescu-Roegen (entropy law constrains economic process), Odum (energy hierarchy constrains institutional forms). The specific application — that a coordination grammar must operate under tighter resource constraints than the distributed-control paradigm it succeeds — is Johar-specific. The foundation is real; the design consequence is Johar's.
docs/research/planning/holding-complexity-diagnostic-split-assessment.md:50:- That tightening energy surplus specifically requires a new coordination grammar (the foundation is confirmed; the design consequence is Johar's)
docs/research/planning/holding-complexity-diagnostic-split-assessment.md:198:**Adjacent promoted families must not lend false certainty.** Legitimacy's strong evidence about authority-consequence coupling does not strengthen the compression-attractor claim. Relational-topology's empirical base does not validate "scaffolded relationality" as one of five required capacities. Human-economy's commitment evidence does not confirm that a new coordination grammar is needed at the civilisational level. Each family's evidence supports only its own claims.
docs/research/connections/johar-neuroplastic-field.md:53:**This essay arrived at Spore independently from outside.** The relation is not influence — it is convergence. Johar is working from governance and institutional design; Spore is working from coordination grammar and agent infrastructure. They are naming the same underlying structure from different sides.
docs/research/connections/johar-neuroplastic-field.md:194:Architectural plasticity (or field neuroplasticity) is the design criterion Spore's coordination grammar is building toward: the capacity of the arrangement to reorganize through experience even when individual LLM components remain fixed.
docs/research/connections/johar-neuroplastic-field.md:213:- **R5**: The standing design rule — "LLMs can propose interpretations; only fields with memory, commitment, and revision can learn" — should be stated explicitly in project-vision. This names the role of LLMs in the coordination grammar as inference infrastructure, not adaptive intelligence, and makes the membrane's division of labor (LLM proposes, governance decides) inspectable as a constitutional commitment. [target: spore.project-vision] [concept: inference-infrastructure] TODO: slug-deferred
docs/research/corpus-review/research-commons-governance.md:52:**Layering breaks down** at three seams. (a) The **rule vs. norm seam**: Crawford & Ostrom (1995, "A Grammar of Institutions," *APSR* 89(3): 582–600) distinguish strategies/norms/rules via the ADICO syntax (Attributes, Deontic, aIm, Conditions, Or else), yet norms without "or else" blur into rules-in-use if sanctions emerge informally. (b) The **polycentric scale seam**: Araral (2014, "Ostrom, Hardin and the commons," *Environmental Science & Policy*) argues the framework works cleanly only for small-N, stationary, observable resources; layering becomes fictive at global scale. (c) The **commoning/rule seam**: Bollier & Helfrich reject the implicit rule-centric ontology of IAD; their "patterns" are not rules in Ostrom's sense but dispositional tendencies, and they explicitly refuse the operational/collective-choice/constitutional stratification as importing a statist governance grammar (*Free, Fair and Alive*, Ch. 2 "OntoShift," §"Complexity Science and Commoning").
docs/research/corpus-review/research-commons-governance.md:121:- Crawford, S. & Ostrom, E. (1995) "A Grammar of Institutions," *APSR* 89(3): 582–600. **[institutional]**.
docs/research/planning/canon-entry-enactment-drafting-batch-1.md:151:## Relationship to the Grammar
docs/research/connections/commons-law-and-charter-lineage.md:63:These lineages compose but do not merge. Magna Carta constrains the sovereign; Charter of the Forest constrains enclosure. A coordination grammar that claims constitutional-artifact lineage must cite the relevant charter, not just "Magna Carta" as generic ancestor.
docs/research/connections/commons-law-and-charter-lineage.md:71:This yields the lesson Spore's `governance-artifacts` must inherit: **constitutional artifacts are fragile**. They do not survive on inscription alone; they require continuous legal-institutional defense against incremental re-enclosure, and continuous mnemonic defense against being collapsed into adjacent, narrower lineages. A coordination grammar that names governance-artifact primitives without naming their fragility is architecturally incomplete.
docs/research/synthesis/planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality.md:110:Spore's project vision should name planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality as a design context for the coordination grammar: the material account of why separable governance assumptions are biophysically eroding and what the coupled regime requires. The entry should include: (a) the biophysical basis — damping loss, coupling thresholds, degenerative volatility as the material conditions that make interdependence operationally dominant, (b) the binding triad — response-time + legitimacy + commitment capacity as the integrated constraint under coupling, (c) planetary option space as the shared good — conditions under which diverse life can adapt, with distribution as a justice criterion, (d) no-subject transformation — institutions are embedded participants, not external controllers, (e) the connection to Spore — the coordination loop is response-time infrastructure, the constitutional layer is legitimacy infrastructure, commitment protocols are commitment-capacity infrastructure, forkability is option-space preservation; together they address the binding triad under planetary conditions, and (f) the falsification test — the thesis weakens if buffers are rebuilt faster than shocks recur and damping capacity increases.
docs/research/synthesis/planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality.md:115:**Primary: candidate pattern** — Planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality names a pattern-level concept for Spore's project vision: the material operating condition in which separable governance assumptions are biophysically eroding and institutional design must internalise the coupled regime. Three sources converge on the same account: damping loss makes interdependence operationally decisive, the subject-object grammar collapses, and the binding constraint becomes the response-time / legitimacy / commitment triad under conditions where delays are cascade multipliers. The pattern provides the material grounding for why Spore's coordination grammar is structurally necessary — not as a design preference but as a response to changed physics.
docs/research/planning/spore-substrate-stack-assessment.md:55:### Layer 1. Artifact Editing And Local Draft State
docs/research/synthesis/worldviews-cohesion-and-systems-change.md:112:Spore's project vision should name worldviews-cohesion-and-systems-change as a design condition for the coordination grammar: the structural account of why systems change involves contest over worldview grammars and what institutional capacity emergent cohesion requires. The entry should include: (a) worldview grammars as the level at which systems change operates — predicted outcomes encode worldviews, civilisational orientations structure agency, the subject-object grammar itself is in play, (b) emergent cohesion as the institutional capacity — not consensus but the ability to maintain coordination and adaptive room across deep worldview differences, measured by relational maturity and evaluated by civilisational optionality, (c) worldview contest as structural, not accidental — fatalism fills the space when contest is suppressed, recursive dynamics between orientations must be designed for, (d) the connection to Spore — sovereignty, contestability, and forkability are worldview-holding mechanisms; the discourse graph makes worldview conflict legible; the learning membrane prevents worldview monopoly, and (e) the open question: what additional mechanisms the grammar needs to ensure cohesion without smuggling in a single worldview.
docs/research/planning/johar-corpus-level-work-plan.md:99:**Why these belong together:** All five name human developmental conditions that Spore's coordination grammar requires but does not provide. Entangled freedom is the ontological ground (what freedom means under entanglement). Care, courage, and presence are the capacities (what agents need to remain perceptually alive). Inter-becoming is the identity process (how selfhood is constituted through participation). Consciousness sovereignty is the subject-formation condition (what replaces compliance). Doubt and plural selfhood are the inner conditions (what makes relational multiplicity inhabitable). Together they form the developmental substrate beneath the grammar.
docs/research/connections/sahely-civil-commons-in-practice.md:31:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-08 empirical case-study paper *"Civil Commons in Practice: Comparative Cases in Water, Health, Education, Ecology, and Governance"* (33-page PDF; Paper 4 in the Life-Coherent Peace sequence; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT GPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, with authorship retained by Sahely per §1 below). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It is a Phase-3 broader-cluster bridge note (lighter ceremony than the Phase-2 anchors): it surfaces resonances against the **already-resolved** Bundle α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and proposes **no admission**. Sahely's relevant canon-pressure was already dispositioned in Bundle α (ADRs 0085–0090); this note cites the resolved state, not any pending DECISION-BRIEF framing. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/corpus-review/research-canonical-layering.md:18:**Layer as boundary of concern.** Evans (2003, Ch. 4, "Layered Architecture") fixes the canonical four-layer stack — **User Interface, Application, Domain, Infrastructure** — and states the motivating principle that "most of the code is not about the domain but about the technology of the software itself" and that "we need to decouple the domain objects from other functions of the system." Mark Richards, in *Software Architecture Patterns* (2015) and *Fundamentals of Software Architecture* (2020, Ch. on the Layered Architecture Style), generalizes this to an **n-tier "technically partitioned"** stack — presentation, business, persistence, database — and names a "closed layer" as one that forces requests through the layer immediately below it, producing "layers of isolation." In this tradition a "layer" is a named region of code with a restricted set of allowed collaborators; it is both an organizational unit for teams (Conway's law is explicitly invoked by Richards) and a unit of substitutability.
docs/research/corpus-review/research-canonical-layering.md:44:**DDD's layered architecture.** Evans (Ch. 4) borrows the four-layer pattern but treats only the domain layer as non-negotiable: "DDD only really requires one isolated layer — the Domain Layer." Everything else may collapse without violating DDD. This is the first hint that in the tradition, layer count is negotiable but the *isolated core* is not.
docs/research/synthesis/priceability-and-system-world.md:35:**spore.connection.johar-priceability** — The refusal to price non-market values does not protect them; it renders them invisible to coordination systems. Priceability is the capacity of systems to perceive and express interdependent value across temporal, spatial, and relational dimensions. Price is reconstructed from scalar extraction signal into a multi-vector coordination grammar. The economy shifts from optimisation to composition — from prediction to learning, from transaction to relational maintenance.
docs/research/synthesis/priceability-and-system-world.md:70:- **Compositional grammar:** Price should be reconstructed from a unidimensional equivalence signal into a multi-vector coordination grammar that translates between incommensurable value forms without reducing them to sameness. This requires systemic sensing, plural valuation protocols, and negotiated allocation (priceability).
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:15:# Reframing Proposal: Spore Identity — Coordination Grammar
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:24:The current line leads with **"infrastructure for collective agency"** — an *agency-enablement* frame. It gestures at the grammar role in its second clause (*"a common grammar for plural, sovereign coordination"*), but the lead under-names what the work across the repo constellation has revealed Spore actually to be: **the upstream coordination grammar that everything else instantiates** — Layer 1 in the four-layer architecture, the substrate the constellation orients around — the grammar that lets local parts keep their own meaning while still composing into a whole that holds together (local sovereignty and global coherence at once).
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:26:This is not a contradiction the way `reframing-pm-canon-scope` was a contradiction. It is an **identity that the work has outgrown.** The 2026-06-02 repo-constellation strategy work (`~/.claude/plans/so-i-had-this-proud-kahn.md` Track B; `docs/research/synthesis/coherence-without-collapse-and-its-projections.md`) established that Spore is turning out to be upstream of Intelligence Commons, bregion, BKC, bioregional-economics, Poietic Match, *and* the non-canon applications (CIE, the RC financing facility, the GPU node network) — each consuming Spore's grammar. The four-layer integration architecture names Spore as **Layer 1 — Grammar**, the source the rest of the constellation orients around. The identity sentence should name that role plainly, in the register the operator already uses for it externally (sheaf.lol's *"coordination grammar for plural / sovereign / local-to-global coherent agentic systems"*; the Schmidt grant bio's *"shared coordination substrates"*).
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:32:Reframe both identity surfaces toward a **math-quiet "coordination grammar / local-to-global coherence" framing (Option A).** The wording leads with *coordination grammar* (operator lean, 2026-06-02 — the most continuous choice, since "grammar" is already canon's own term and matches "Layer 1 — Grammar" in the architecture) and names *holding local sovereignty and global coherence at once* as what the grammar is for.
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:39:> "Spore is a coordination grammar for plural, sovereign systems — one that holds local sovereignty and global coherence at once, across scales and scopes."
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:42:> "Spore is a coordination grammar for plural, sovereign systems — one that holds local sovereignty and global coherence at once, across scales and scopes: it lets autonomous parts keep their own meaning while still composing into a whole that holds together. As an infrastructure for collective agency, it operates across the normative commitments that shape how agents see, value, know, and act (ontological, axiological, epistemological, practical)…"
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:45:> "Spore follows the same logic — a shared coordination grammar that can land across projects, grow in different forms, and stay coherent across them without requiring centralization."
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:55:5. **`"coordination grammar"` is the chosen lead noun; `"infrastructure for collective agency"` is retained as secondary phrasing, not the lead** (resolved 2026-06-02) — under a grammar-lead the separate *"a common grammar for…"* clause is folded into the lead, and *"infrastructure for collective agency"* moves to a secondary clause in the project-vision paragraph (*"As an infrastructure for collective agency, it operates across the normative commitments…"*). README.md:7 stays lean (tagline only; no secondary clause).
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:59:This change exceeds ordinary canon-review ADR scope under **FR-1 criterion 5 (changes the definition of canon scope), read at the identity layer.** The opening sentence of `project-vision.md` (a `doc_kind: vision` constitutional doc) is the canon's self-definition. Repositioning Spore from *"infrastructure for collective agency"* to *"a coordination grammar (local-to-global coherence)"* changes what the canon says it **is**, and its role relative to the downstream-aligned (IC, PM) and peer-instance-family (bregion, BKC, bioregional-economics) constellation that now treats Spore as upstream. **FR-2 (ambiguity rule)** is explicit: a change that *"alters a layer's identity"* defaults to foundational reframing, *"not downward."*
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:63:**Honest narrowing.** This is the *narrowest* canon-scope sub-case — the self-description wording, not the governed-surface boundary that `reframing-pm-canon-scope` re-drew (which re-layered a doc out of canon). It is therefore lighter than that precedent. It still belongs here because (a) FR-2 routes it here, (b) the operator elected the heavier ceremony for the constitutional identity line, and (c) the cost of getting the one orienting sentence wrong is high: it propagates to the README, sheaf.lol, grant materials, and every downstream *"Spore is…"* citation. The 7-day cooling-off is cheap insurance against a hasty edit to the line the whole constellation reads first.
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:85:  excerpt: "a shared coordination grammar that can land across projects, grow in different forms, and remain interoperable without requiring centralization."
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:86:  contributes: Shows the "coordination grammar" framing — the chosen lead noun — is ALREADY in the README body one paragraph below the identity line; the reframe surfaces into the identity line what the canon already says about itself.
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:113:  excerpt: "shared coordination substrates: memory, commitments, evidence, provenance, permissions, signals, and boundary structures…" / "coordination infrastructure … for plural, multi-stakeholder environments."
docs/research/planning/reframing/reframing-spore-identity.md:170:- *Lead noun* → **coordination grammar** (most continuous; canon's own word). `"substrate"` / `"infrastructure"` noted as alternatives but not chosen.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-claude-opus-4-7-2026-04-22.md:161:**My call: stronger than both prior audits — delete.** Both audits suggest softening to "cross-scale motifs" or "recurrent coordination questions." This is still too much. The self-similarity claim at `constitutional-artifacts-and-graph-projections.md:67-73` has no content beyond "a node can be treated as a point from outside and as a graph from inside." This is true of literally any aggregating system — organisms, teams, states, galaxies. It is not a property specific to Spore's coordination grammar; it is a property of the concept of aggregation. Naming it as a foundational principle is naming a tautology.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-claude-opus-4-7-2026-04-22.md:203:**My call: agree with both audits that the issue is real; add a further diagnosis.** The canon describes a universal-scope coordination grammar but operationally requires tech-fluent metadata authoring. Both audits note the gap. What neither audit names: **the canon's adoption model is radically underdeveloped relative to the rest of the canon**. The canon has multi-page sections on holons, semilattices, polycentric governance — and a half-page section on adoption. Adoption is not a side issue for a grammar that claims universal coordination scope; it is the central empirical test. If the canon cannot tell you how a non-tech-fluent community would adopt it (answer: they can't, currently), the universality claim is false in the only sense that matters.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-claude-opus-4-7-2026-04-22.md:242:Without failure-mode specifications, the canon is describing a coordination grammar that has never been tested under adversarial conditions. This is a bigger gap than any of the naming issues the prior audit focused on.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-claude-opus-4-7-2026-04-22.md:369:  What would change my mind: a case study of BKC/Octo that is operationally detailed enough to show the object-level coordination grammar has earned specification voice at scale. The roadmap honesty at `roadmap.md:15-32` actually supports my view here.
tmp/canon-audit-independent-second-opinion-claude-opus-4-7-2026-04-22.md:405:Whether Spore wants to do this is an operator question, not an auditor question. What the canon currently is, honestly named, is *a promising coordination grammar with well-developed self-evolution machinery, whose foundational layer has not yet been tested against its own questions*. That framing is an honest middle between the prior audit's "overclaimed specification" and the canon's own current voice.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-prep-batch-3-holding-complexity-diagnostic.md:41:- **Energetic/material constraint as secondary context (if included).** The thermodynamic foundation is directly corroborated: coordination has irreducible energetic costs (Tainter), the economic process is entropy transformation (Georgescu-Roegen), energy hierarchy constrains institutional forms (Odum). Three independent traditions. The application — that a coordination grammar must operate under tighter resource constraints than distributed control — is Johar's design inference. **If energetic constraint enters the diagnostic at all**, it can only appear as: "coordination has thermodynamic costs and surplus is tightening, which constrains the institutional forms available for adaptive response." It cannot appear as: "the grammar must be designed for tighter constraints." The foundation is confirmed; the design consequence stays out.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-prep-batch-3-holding-complexity-diagnostic.md:82:- The energetic/material constraint as secondary context: coordination has thermodynamic costs, energy surplus is tightening, and this constrains what institutional forms are available for adaptive response (Tainter, Georgescu-Roegen, Odum — foundation confirmed). The claim that this specifically requires a new coordination grammar is Johar's design inference and stays outside the diagnostic proper.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-prep-batch-3-holding-complexity-diagnostic.md:187:**Adjacent promoted families must not lend false certainty.** Legitimacy's strong evidence about authority-consequence coupling does not strengthen the compression-attractor claim. Relational-topology's empirical base does not validate "scaffolded relationality." Human-economy's commitment evidence does not confirm that a new coordination grammar is needed at the civilisational level. Each family stands on its own evidence.
docs/research/connections/sahely-xin-heart-mind.md:38:# Sahely (2018-06-20) Xin (The Heart-Mind) and Feeling Tones ↔ Spore Substrate-Grammar Map
docs/research/synthesis/agility-contribution-and-organizing.md:78:- **Grammar as platform for adaptive coordination:** The grammar's commitment protocols, discourse graph, and holon architecture are the platform that invests optionality into the coordination environment. Agents who participate through the grammar are more agile than agents coordinating ad hoc (infrastructure-agility).
