docs/research/connections/sahely-word-becomes-flesh.md:41:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-25 white paper *"When the Word Becomes Flesh: Organized Religion, Artificial Intelligence, and the Primordial Test of Life-Coherence"* (30-page PDF; bsahely.com; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). It surfaces resonance against Spore's **post-Bundle-α** canon state (concepts-yaml v24; four cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and cites the *resolved* Bundle-α ADRs where this post's themes were already dispositioned. **It admits nothing.** Per single-source rigor, Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus; cross-post recurrence within his corpus is **not** independent evidence and no convergence is claimed here. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`) — no write-side recommendations.
docs/research/connections/sahely-economy-answerable-to-life.md:32:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Dr. Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-14 academic paper *"An Economy Answerable to Life: Beyond GDP, Unequal Exchange, and the Life-Coherent Reordering of Progress"* (36-page PDF; bsahely.com; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT GPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely per §1). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the 3-layer intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). This is a **Phase 3** lighter-ceremony note: the post-Bundle-α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) has already RESOLVED the canon-pressure this post's themes touch — life-value, the master-substitution trap, and maintenance-economics all received their dispositions during Bundle α (ADRs 0085–0090, 2026-05-23 → 05-29). This note therefore **admits nothing**; it maps the post's themes onto already-resolved canon and records cross-tradition reinforcement honestly. Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus; **cross-post recurrence within his corpus is not independent evidence** and is not treated as convergence. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per `feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md` — no write-side recommendation for IC / bregion / BKC / PM.
docs/research/synthesis/compositional-field-architecture.md:74:The column-by-column alignment is not decorative. Each project is a functioning instance of the same five-layer architecture at different scale, content, and governance. What Spore's coordination grammar does for cross-project learning is the same architectural move Ruddick's commitment-pool formalism does for economic flow and Waka's compositional witness taxonomy does for perceptual provenance. The pattern is one thing. The instantiations are many.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-packet-batch-1.md:110:> Language compresses reality into categories that produce a structural sense of sufficiency, terminating inquiry before truth evaluation begins. This is not a cognitive error but a property of how categories operate in institutional contexts: paradigms determine what can be perceived as a problem, stabilised facts become invisible through their own success, and organisations treat enacted categories as given reality. Four independent traditions confirm this mechanism. The corrective is institutional, not individual: structural revisability, error-finding incentives, and recursive inquiry keep categories open to revision. The replication crisis demonstrates both the failure mode and the structural reform. [mechanism confirmed: Peirce, Kuhn, Latour, Weick; case: replication crisis] Johar contributes the specific claim that naming is the upstream trigger, and proposes the claim lifecycle, discourse graph, and attestation decay as general-purpose anti-closure infrastructure for coordination grammar. [design contribution] Whether these specific mechanisms resist closure at institutional scale, and whether automated language production amplifies closure risk, are open design hypotheses. [design hypothesis]
tmp/handoff-prompt-co-reader-meta-learning-field-design.md:21:- **Spore canon** at `~/projects/spore/` — coordination grammar; 35 canon-decisions; 14 foundation docs; 5 positioning docs; 7 patterns; yaml v20; validator 9 errors / 30 warnings EXACT held throughout; zero rollbacks
docs/research/connections/johar-presence-engineering.md:83:Spore's architecture is built around conditions rather than scripts. The coordination grammar does not prescribe what agents should do; it provides the structural conditions under which coordination can emerge. The commitment lifecycle does not dictate outcomes; it creates conditions for accountability. Discourse-as-governance does not enforce decisions; it creates conditions for structured reasoning.
docs/research/connections/johar-presence-engineering.md:101:Johar's fourth characteristic -- craft-enabled responsiveness -- describes "embodied epistemology, a method of knowing through doing." This is the dimension where Spore's grammar is thinnest. The coordination grammar is deliberative: agents sense, interpret, claim, attest, intend, commit, coordinate, act, revise. This loop privileges the propositional-deliberative mode of intelligence.
docs/research/connections/johar-presence-engineering.md:130:Spore's coordination grammar is systematically on the coherence side of the control/coherence divide. The grammar provides conditions for coordination rather than prescribing behavior. This orientation is implicit across commitment-pooling, discourse-as-governance, and the learning membrane, but is not stated as a named design principle.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-packet-batch-3-holding-complexity-diagnostic.md:75:- **Energetic/material constraint as secondary context (if included at all).** The thermodynamic foundation is directly corroborated: coordination has irreducible energetic costs (Tainter), the economic process is entropy transformation (Georgescu-Roegen), energy hierarchy constrains institutional forms (Odum). Three independent traditions. The application — that a coordination grammar must operate under tighter resource constraints than distributed control — is Johar's design inference. If this appears in the diagnostic at all, it can only appear as: "coordination has thermodynamic costs and surplus is tightening, which constrains the institutional forms available for adaptive response." It cannot appear as a core pillar or a design directive.
docs/research/planning/promotion-review-packet-batch-3-holding-complexity-diagnostic.md:183:**Adjacent promoted families must not lend false certainty.** Legitimacy's strong evidence about authority-consequence coupling does not strengthen the compression-attractor claim. Relational-topology's empirical base does not validate "scaffolded relationality." Human-economy's commitment evidence does not confirm that a new coordination grammar is needed at the civilisational level. Each family stands on its own evidence.
docs/research/synthesis/hyperstition-governance.md:37:**spore.connection.hyperstition** — Establishes the structural parallel between hyperstition theory and Spore's coordination grammar. Core argument: Spore adds accountability, contestability, and evidence requirements that the hyperstition mechanism alone lacks. Maps intent pressure to the belief-encoding force in hyperstition dynamics. Stance toward canon: **clarify** existing terms in project-vision and commitment-pooling. All 3 claims support the review claims.
docs/research/synthesis/hyperstition-governance.md:67:Spore's constitutional commitments assume a view from within the coordination grammar. What looks like authorized boundary crossing from inside a commitment pool may look like illegitimate expansion from outside. The criteria are scope-relative, not universal. This challenges any promotion that would frame Spore's safeguards as sufficient rather than provisional.
docs/research/synthesis/hyperstition-governance.md:79:This claim from the constructive-hyperstition note *sounds* supportive but was projected as an opposes edge because the note's overall disposition is "no change" — the criteria are offered as candidates, explicitly framed as carrying Spore's design assumptions. A different coordination grammar might draw the line differently. The opposition is epistemological: the criteria are theory-laden, not neutral.
docs/research/synthesis/hyperstition-governance.md:95:- **spore.project-vision** — Clarify how hyperstition dynamics relate to the project's coordination grammar. The vision doc describes the coordination ecology but does not name the hyperstition parallel.
docs/research/synthesis/hyperstition-governance.md:102:Clarify existing terms. The hyperstition comparison illuminates what Spore's coordination grammar is doing without proposing structural changes. The tensions are real but they are about completeness, not about error — the grammar's safeguards are relevant; the question is whether they are sufficient.
