docs/research/synthesis/coherence-without-collapse-and-its-projections.md:71:1. **Grammar (Spore)** — the coordination grammar; the design move above + (backstage) the sheaf lens as research. Upstream; never forked; never a propagation target.
docs/research/synthesis/coherence-without-collapse-and-its-projections.md:89:- **Earned (frontstage-ready now):** the *design move* (route through coherence; obstruction-is-information; don't-flatten-sovereignty); the four-layer architecture (it's the existing topology); the two-register discipline; "local-to-global coherence" as plain language for what the grammar already does.
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/compass_artifact_wf-55fa505b-3b6d-438c-8a06-c71280db115d_text_markdown.md:7:**Layer as boundary of concern.** Evans (2003, Ch. 4, "Layered Architecture") fixes the canonical four-layer stack — **User Interface, Application, Domain, Infrastructure** — and states the motivating principle that "most of the code is not about the domain but about the technology of the software itself" and that "we need to decouple the domain objects from other functions of the system." Mark Richards, in *Software Architecture Patterns* (2015) and *Fundamentals of Software Architecture* (2020, Ch. on the Layered Architecture Style), generalizes this to an **n-tier "technically partitioned"** stack — presentation, business, persistence, database — and names a "closed layer" as one that forces requests through the layer immediately below it, producing "layers of isolation." In this tradition a "layer" is a named region of code with a restricted set of allowed collaborators; it is both an organizational unit for teams (Conway's law is explicitly invoked by Richards) and a unit of substitutability.
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/compass_artifact_wf-55fa505b-3b6d-438c-8a06-c71280db115d_text_markdown.md:33:**DDD's layered architecture.** Evans (Ch. 4) borrows the four-layer pattern but treats only the domain layer as non-negotiable: "DDD only really requires one isolated layer — the Domain Layer." Everything else may collapse without violating DDD. This is the first hint that in the tradition, layer count is negotiable but the *isolated core* is not.
docs/research/connections/sahely-toward-life-coherent-peace.md:53:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-21 white paper *"Toward Life-Coherent Peace in the Middle East: Sacred Memory, Structural Violence, and the Protection of the Life-Ground"* (41 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). It is **Wave-3 #7 of Phase 2** — authored **after operator ratification** of the Phase 2 Wave-1+2 DECISION-BRIEF (`tmp/sahely-corpus-canon-pressure-decision-brief-2026-05-22.md`). Per the 3-layer separation discipline (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`), this bridge note operates at **Layer 1.5 in supporting-evidence mode**: it documents how this anchor **deepens already-ratified dispositions** (C1 R-Trap-cluster ADMIT, C2 R-Care-cluster scope-condition, C3 R-McMurtry-substrate-cluster ADMIT, C6 R-Civil-Commons ADMIT standalone, C13 R-Perception-as-power scope-condition F4) rather than re-litigating Layer-2 verdicts. Any new candidates surfaced (see §3 below) carry disposition `framing-note-only` with explicit flag for **operator-elective DECISION-BRIEF refinement** — they do not self-admit and they do not pre-commit canon. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); no write-side recommendations against IC / bregion / BKC / PM.
docs/research/connections/sahely-toward-life-coherent-peace.md:185:This anchor's C-13 *life-ground enumeration for Middle East* is the most-specific operational articulation of UHLN (Universal Human Life Necessities) Sahely has produced in the corpus reviewed at Layer 1.5:
docs/research/connections/sahely-toward-life-coherent-peace.md:361:- **3-layer separation discipline preserved**: bridge note is Layer 1.5; no Layer-2 verdict re-litigation; no Layer-3 ADR drafting; new candidate observations flagged for operator-elective DECISION-BRIEF refinement only.
docs/research/connections/johar-biophysically-entering.md:42:The essay's primary contribution is making the systems condition material rather than interpretive. The shift from "object world" to "systems world" is not a change in lens but a change in the physics of propagation. Coupling thresholds fall not because we have become more aware but because damping capacity is depleting. For Spore, this grounds the grammar's design rationale in material conditions: the coordination grammar is necessary because the buffered, separable world in which simpler governance sufficed is biophysically eroding.
docs/research/connections/johar-biophysically-entering.md:67:- **R1**: Spore's project vision should name planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality as a design context for the coordination grammar: the material account of why separable governance assumptions are biophysically eroding and what the coupled regime requires. The entry should include: (a) the biophysical basis — coupling thresholds fall as damping depletes, making latent interdependence operationally dominant, (b) degenerative volatility — persistent variance with incomplete recovery, structurally cumulative rather than episodic, (c) endogenous buffer loss — optimisation as systematic thinning of the slack that enabled separability, (d) the binding triad — response-time + legitimacy + commitment capacity as the integrated constraint under coupling, and (e) the connection to Spore — the coordination loop is response-time infrastructure, the constitutional layer is legitimacy infrastructure, commitment protocols are commitment-capacity infrastructure; together they address the binding triad. [target: spore.project-vision] [concept: planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality] TODO: slug-deferred
docs/research/connections/johar-biophysically-entering.md:77:**Primary: candidate pattern** — Planetary-systems-and-biophysical-reality names a pattern-level concept for Spore's project vision: the material condition in which the separable "object world" approximation is eroding and the coupled "systems world" regime demands new coordination infrastructure. The essay is technically precise (1516w, with a falsification section), directly names commitment protocols and legitimacy production as governance infrastructure, and provides the material grounding for why Spore's coordination grammar is structurally necessary.
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/compass_artifact_wf-60459b5e-71c9-4034-ace3-89d506375970_text_markdown.md:41:**Layering breaks down** at three seams. (a) The **rule vs. norm seam**: Crawford & Ostrom (1995, "A Grammar of Institutions," *APSR* 89(3): 582–600) distinguish strategies/norms/rules via the ADICO syntax (Attributes, Deontic, aIm, Conditions, Or else), yet norms without "or else" blur into rules-in-use if sanctions emerge informally. (b) The **polycentric scale seam**: Araral (2014, "Ostrom, Hardin and the commons," *Environmental Science & Policy*) argues the framework works cleanly only for small-N, stationary, observable resources; layering becomes fictive at global scale. (c) The **commoning/rule seam**: Bollier & Helfrich reject the implicit rule-centric ontology of IAD; their "patterns" are not rules in Ostrom's sense but dispositional tendencies, and they explicitly refuse the operational/collective-choice/constitutional stratification as importing a statist governance grammar (*Free, Fair and Alive*, Ch. 2 "OntoShift," §"Complexity Science and Commoning").
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/compass_artifact_wf-60459b5e-71c9-4034-ace3-89d506375970_text_markdown.md:110:- Crawford, S. & Ostrom, E. (1995) "A Grammar of Institutions," *APSR* 89(3): 582–600. **[institutional]**.
docs/research/connections/sahely-keeping-life-coherence-alive.md:43:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-19 paper *"Keeping Life-Coherence Alive: A Maturanan Reflection on Distinction Capture and the Mythic Traps of Civilizational Repair"* (68 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). It is a **descriptive** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the 3-layer intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`): bridge note surfaces canon-pressure CANDIDATES; honest-rigor cluster-counting and ADMIT/DECLINE verdicts belong in the Layer 2 DECISION-BRIEF (`tmp/sahely-corpus-canon-pressure-decision-brief-2026-05-22.md`, authored separately by orchestrator). Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`) — it makes no recommendation for write-side action at IC/bregion/BKC/PM.
docs/research/connections/sahely-keeping-life-coherence-alive.md:68:The 2026-05-21 *Maturana-Informed Viability Grammar* (Wave-1 anchor #1) surfaced an initial R-Trap candidate against ADR-0048 substitution-trap via C-12 of that paper (*"a viability grammar becomes life-incoherent if it is used to dominate, accuse, or negate; the grammar must apply its own question to itself"*). That candidate was disposed `canon-pressure-DECISION-BRIEF` and flagged with the cross-anchor note *"anchor #4 (Keeping Life-Coherence Alive — Maturanan Reflection on Distinction Capture and Mythic Traps) directly addresses distinction-capture and is the natural cross-reference for substitution-trap resonance — that anchor will deepen the cluster-counting substrate before DECISION-BRIEF assesses."*
