docs/research/connections/sahely-keeping-life-coherence-alive.md:309:**Cluster 2 — Maturanan-Sahely-lineage (this anchor + Wave-1 anchors + Sahely's 11-trap synthesis).** Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-19 *Keeping Life-Coherence Alive* + 2026-05-21 *Maturana-Informed Viability Grammar* C-12 recursive-safeguard, integrating Maturana (biology of cognition; conservation; structural coupling) + McMurtry (life-value / civil commons) + Galtung (structural violence / cultural violence) with mythic-symbol categorical scaffolding. Operational concern: *coherence-grammar's use is the operational site of its life-coherence-or-incoherence; corrective distinction can be captured into the domination it was introduced to correct.* Cluster surface vocabulary: Golden Calf Trap / Trojan Horse Trap / 11-trap mythic-diagnostic grammar / recursive life-coherence audit. Cluster operational concern: corrective-distinction-becomes-the-capture-it-was-introduced-to-correct. **Surface match: differentiated (different terminology). Operational concern match: complete (same failure-shape named).** Structurally independent from Cluster 1 by source-tradition (biology-of-cognition lineage vs Sufi-organizational lineage); demonstrates ≥2-tradition convergence on operational concern.
tmp/p2p-wiki-synthesis-2026-04-20.md:15:- Spore as multi-agent coordination grammar, collective-agency substrate, federation surface, and portability claim
docs/research/synthesis/holding-complexity-beyond-control.md:21:A synthesis note on the holding-complexity-beyond-control concept, drawn from the Johar complexity intake (Batches 1–2) with cross-theme seed evidence from governance, infrastructure, and intelligence intakes. This is the strongest complexity family (7 pre-synthesis sources, 24 supports) and the most heavily seeded concept in the entire Johar corpus intake. It names the civilisational structural condition that makes Spore's coordination grammar necessary: complexity cannot be adequately handled by control, prediction, or optimisation alone. The relevant capacity is the ability to hold complexity — to coordinate, learn, relate, and remain coherent without collapsing into authoritarian compression, simplification, or chaotic decomposition.
docs/research/synthesis/holding-complexity-beyond-control.md:124:Spore's project vision should name holding-complexity-beyond-control as a design context for the coordination grammar: the civilisational structural condition that makes the grammar's adaptive mechanisms necessary, the two default attractors the grammar must resist, and the institutional capacities the grammar must provide. The entry should include: (a) the failure of control — representational inadequacy, energetic tightening, permanence dissolution, and self-sealing expectation as mechanisms by which control loses adequacy, (b) the two attractors — authoritarian compression and chaotic decomposition as pathways the grammar's design must avoid, (c) the five structural capacities — adaptive coordination, complexity-handling capacity, scaffolded relationality, interdependent sovereignty, and anti-fragility through learning — and their mapping to existing grammar mechanisms, (d) civilisational optionality as the evaluative criterion — institutions judged by whether they widen or narrow the legitimate response space, and (e) the thermodynamic implication — the grammar must operate under tighter resource constraints than the distributed control paradigm it succeeds.
docs/research/planning/mediation-section-draft-spec.md:40:- **Paragraph 2 — Grammar grounding.** Shows that the grammar already practices mediation-over-demarcation through four concrete mechanisms: authorized boundary crossing, federation exchange rules, holon membrane functions, and (implicitly) the learning membrane. Names the principle as making explicit what these mechanisms share.
docs/research/connections/sahely-biology-of-love-to-governance.md:45:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-05 white paper *"From the Biology of Love to Life-Coherent Governance: A Maturanan, Galtungian, and McMurtrian Framework for Structural Violence, Civil Commons, and Non-Forcing Politics"* (29 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT GPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). This is a **Phase 3 lighter-ceremony** bridge note, authored *after* the Bundle α canon-discipline arc closed (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090). Its themes are therefore mapped to the **resolved** canon state — the canon-pressure this paper carries was already metabolized by ADRs 0085–0090 — not to any pending DECISION-BRIEF. No admission is proposed here; nothing in this note is admit-shaped. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`).
