docs/research/connections/sahely-credit-creation-system.md:43:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2017-05-06 blog post **"Is our credit creation system the father of all pathogenic human interferences?"** (HTML; `bsahely.com`; "TOWARD LIFE-KNOWLEDGE" banner). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake program. It is **Phase 3** of the Sahely intake (lighter-ceremony broader-cluster pass following the Bundle α canon-discipline arc, which closed 2026-05-29 across ADRs 0085→0090). **It admits nothing.** This post is **FOUNDATION-ERA (2017–2018) — pre the Dec-2022+ AI-co-authored white-paper explosion**: `ai_co_authored: false`, **Sahely-original (pre-AI)**, single first-person essay. The canon-pressure this post anticipates (a decade early) was already dispositioned by Bundle α; this note cites the **resolved** canon state (concepts-yaml v24; four cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and maps the post's themes onto already-admitted vocabulary. Per **single-source rigor**, Sahely is one author corpus; this 2017 post foreshadowing his later (2025–2026) white-paper framings is **not** independent evidence — it is the same author's earlier articulation, and recurrence within his corpus re-counts no clusters and re-opens no ADRs. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per `feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`; it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/connections/sahely-global-projections-galtung.md:28:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side descriptive substrate-resonance bridge note for a Bichara Sahely blog post that **reposts** Johan Galtung's 1996 monograph *Global Projections of Deep-Rooted U.S. Pathologies* (Institute of International Studies / TRANSCEND) via a NotebookLM-generated structured abstract. It is a Phase-3, **framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`): the note maps a post's themes onto **already-resolved** Spore canon (post-Bundle-α; concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090). It surfaces **no** new canon-pressure, proposes **no** admission, and runs **no** cluster-counting verdicts. Single-source rigor applies twice over here: (a) Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus, and cross-post recurrence within it is not independent evidence; and (b) the substantive philosophical claims belong to **Galtung (1996)**, not Sahely — Sahely is the curator/reposter, NotebookLM the abstraction layer. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/connections/sahely-global-projections-galtung.md:102:C1's myths (Manifest Destiny; the "Trinity" of Judeo-Christianity / Free Markets / Democracy) and C2's DMA syndrome (dichotomy → Manicheism → Armageddon) are textbook specimens of two ADR-0085 trap shapes: a **mythic-trap** (a glamorizing narrative substituting for honest self-account — the `golden-calf-trap` is the SHAPE-OF ADR-0048's substitution-trap, the worshipped-image standing in for the living thing) and **grammar-used-to-dominate** (Us-vs-Them carved into "watertight parts" then moralized Good-vs-Evil, a coordination grammar weaponized for domination rather than coordination). The DMA "Armageddon" limb — that tension *must* resolve through final violent confrontation — is the grammar's domination-mode made explicit. No new trap-shape is surfaced; ADR-0085's vocabulary already covers these.
