docs/research/2026-04-03/podcast-context-spore-agent-commons.md:760:Open Civics names "extitutions" — self-organizing frameworks with permeable boundaries. In the coordination grammar, an extitution is a holon with explicit membrane operations. The grammar makes extitutions buildable, not just describable.
docs/research/2026-04-03/synthesis.md:156:4. **Epistemic justice analysis** — Fricker's testimonial/hermeneutical injustice applied to the grammar itself. The Grammar Extension Protocol (allowing communities to propose new grammar elements from below) is a design requirement Report A doesn't surface.
docs/research/2026-04-03/synthesis.md:165:   - Grammar normativity paradox (enabling coordination constrains expression)
docs/research/2026-04-03/synthesis.md:207:12. **Grammar Extension Protocol** — formal mechanism for communities to propose new grammar elements. *(Report B, epistemic justice requirement)*
docs/research/2026-04-03/chatgpt-deep-research-prompt-2026-04.md:25:Treat the uploaded files as the primary internal corpus. Use current web research to compare Spore against adjacent projects, standards, and theories. Your job is not to summarize everything you find. Your job is to identify what would most help Spore evolve into a more legible, adoptable, and structurally sound coordination grammar.
docs/research/2026-04-03/chatgpt-deep-research-prompt-2026-04.md:30:- Spore is a coordination grammar and pattern language for plural, sovereign coordination across scales.
docs/research/connections/sahely-metanoia-historical-jesus.md:31:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-03-12 paper *"Metanoia and the Historical Jesus: Inner Transformation, Civilizational Misinterpretation, and the Institutionalization of a Mystical Teaching"* (78pp; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT 5.3 + Gemini + NotebookLM-aided figures). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact (Layer 1.5). It surfaces no canon-pressure and proposes no admission. The canon-citation map below references the **resolved post-Bundle-α state** (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090); the Sahely-corpus canon-pressure that *was* live in the Phase-2 DECISION-BRIEF has already been dispositioned in ADRs 0085–0090. This note's job is only to map a single later Sahely post onto the already-resolved canon, honestly and without overclaiming. **Single-source rigor:** Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus; this paper's recurrence of themes seen in earlier Sahely papers is **not** independent cross-tradition evidence and is never counted as cluster-support here.
docs/research/connections/sahely-metanoia-historical-jesus.md:94:No row is canon-pressure: every theme this paper raises either (a) sits at the individual-spiritual-development layer adjacent-but-cross-layer to Spore's coordination grammar (per extraction R-5), or (b) maps onto territory the Bundle α ADRs already dispositioned for the Sahely corpus as a whole.
docs/research/connections/sahely-metanoia-historical-jesus.md:147:Every R-claim is **framing-note-only**. No canon-pressure surfaced; no admission proposed. The paper sits at the individual-spiritual-development / civilizational-ethics layer, adjacent-but-cross-layer to Spore's coordination grammar (extraction R-5). Single-source rigor preserved throughout: this one AI-co-authored paper — and its internal cross-tradition comparison (C7) — is never counted as independent convergence evidence. Spore canon at post-Bundle-α plateau is untouched by this note (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions); this is a single Spore-side connection artifact with no canon-touching execution.
tmp/sahely-p4-payloads/req-27-living.json:1:{"name": "Sahely 2026-05-27 Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease (Phase-4 catch-up)", "content": "This white paper derives neuropsychiatric disease from disturbances in \"living coherence\" across five interdependent layers \u2014 autopoiesis, structural coupling, emotioning, felt interiority, and emotional sentience \u2014 arguing that mental disorder cannot be adequately understood through any single lens (brain disease, chemical imbalance, cognitive distortion, trauma, social stress, or diagnostic category) because each is only a partial truth and the missing integrative layer is the living process itself. It reframes incoherence not as personal failing or moral deficit but as a sign that life conditions, regulatory capacity, or organism-world coupling have become nonviable, and recasts symptoms as messages of disturbed viability that treatment must listen to before correcting. Its original methodological contribution is a \"Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar\" (Constraint, Margin, State, Disturbance, Perception, Regulation, Options) offering a disciplined transdiagnostic method for locating how coherence breaks down and where repair may begin, with healing redefined as the restoration of viable self-regulation, truthful feeling, legitimate relation, expanded options, and renewed participation in a livable world. Epistemic status: this is an AI-co-authored synthesis (ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking as dialogical research/editorial assistant plus NotebookLM per the record, with all substantive judgment reserved to the author); it is a single-source document drawn from one author's corpus and is not independently corroborated.", "source_description": "Sahely white-paper (AI-co-authored), bsahely.com", "source_document": "https://bsahely.com/2026/05/27/living-coherence-and-neuropsychiatric-disease-autopoiesis-structural-coupling-emotioning-and-emotional-sentience-as-foundations-for-a-transdiagnostic-psychiatry-chatgpt-5-5-thinking-and-notebook/", "facts": [{"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "AUTHORED_BY", "object": "Bichara Sahely", "fact_text": "The white paper 'Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease' was authored by Bichara Sahely (BSc, MBBS, DM), with AI editorial assistance from ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking and NotebookLM; the author retains all substantive judgment and final responsibility.", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Neuropsychiatric disease is derived from disturbances in living coherence across five foundational layers: autopoiesis, structural coupling, emotioning, felt interiority, and emotional sentience.", "fact_text": "The paper's central derivational thesis is that neuropsychiatric disease can be derived from disturbances in living coherence across five foundational layers \u2014 autopoiesis, structural coupling, emotioning, felt interiority, and emotional sentience (Abstract, pdf-p2).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "INTRODUCES", "object": "living coherence", "fact_text": "The paper introduces 'living coherence' as the capacity of a living system to conserve its organization, maintain viable relation with its medium, regulate its bodily-affective orientation, inhabit its own felt condition, and participate in meaningful worlds \u2014 presented as a derivable framework, not a holistic slogan (\u00a71 Introduction, pdf-p7).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "INTRODUCES", "object_literal": "Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar: Constraint, Margin, State, Disturbance, Perception, Regulation, and Options", "fact_text": "The paper introduces the Seven-Primitives Clinical Grammar \u2014 Constraint, Margin, State, Disturbance, Perception, Regulation, and Options \u2014 as a disciplined transdiagnostic method for assessing how living coherence breaks down and how it may be restored (Abstract + \u00a710, pdf-p2/p16).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "REFRAMES", "object_literal": "Incoherence is not a personal failing or moral deficit but a sign that life conditions, regulatory capacity, or organism-world coupling have become nonviable.", "fact_text": "The paper reframes incoherence de-moralizingly: it is not a personal failing or moral deficit, but a sign that life conditions, regulatory capacity, or organism-world coupling have become nonviable (Abstract, pdf-p2).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Mental disorder cannot be adequately understood through any single lens; brain disease, chemical imbalance, cognitive distortion, trauma response, social stress, and diagnostic category are all partial truths, and the missing integrative layer is the living process itself.", "fact_text": "The paper claims mental disorder cannot be adequately understood through any single lens \u2014 brain disease, chemical imbalance, cognitive distortion, trauma, social stress, or diagnostic category are all partial truths \u2014 and the missing integrative layer is the living process itself: the organism as a self-producing, structurally coupled, emotionally oriented, interoceptively felt, meaning-making unity (Executive Summary, pdf-p6).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Healing cannot be reduced to symptom reduction; it must also restore viable self-regulation, truthful feeling, legitimate relation, expanded options, and renewed participation in a livable world.", "fact_text": "The paper claims healing cannot be reduced to symptom reduction; it must also restore viable self-regulation, truthful feeling, legitimate relation, expanded options, and renewed participation in a livable world (Executive Summary, pdf-p6).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Symptoms become messages of disturbed viability; the emotional system is attempting to regulate significance, so treatment must listen before it corrects.", "fact_text": "The paper claims that if emotion is understood as a self-regulatory sense, then symptoms become messages of disturbed viability; even when an emotion's interpretation is inaccurate, the emotional system is still attempting to regulate significance, so treatment must listen before it corrects (\u00a78, pdf-p14).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "ENGAGES_CONCEPT", "object": "autopoiesis", "fact_text": "The paper engages autopoiesis as its first principle, defining the living organism as a materially open but organizationally closed, self-producing unity whose processes recursively produce the components and boundary conditions that constitute it; clinically it provides the first question \u2014 what is the living system struggling to conserve? (\u00a74, pdf-p11-12).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "ENGAGES_CONCEPT", "object": "structural coupling", "fact_text": "The paper engages structural coupling as its second principle \u2014 the recurrent history through which organism and medium become sufficiently congruent for living to continue \u2014 arguing the person and world co-develop through histories of coupling rather than the person simply being located in an environment (\u00a75, pdf-p12).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "DISTINGUISHES", "object_literal": "Valence (better/worse for viability, present in primitive organisms via chemotaxis and stress responses) is distinguished from emotioning (in animals, bodily dispositions that open and close domains of possible action).", "fact_text": "The paper distinguishes valence \u2014 the better/worse significance of conditions for viability, present even in primitive organisms (bacterial chemotaxis, stress responses, quorum sensing) without conscious feeling \u2014 from emotioning, which in animals is the flow of bodily dispositions specifying domains of possible action (\u00a76, pdf-p13).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Rationality is never emotionally neutral; reasoning operates within a domain of action already opened by emotion, so a proposal heard in trust differs from one heard in humiliation.", "fact_text": "The paper claims rationality is never emotionally neutral: reasoning operates within a domain of action already opened by emotion, so a proposal heard in trust is not the same as one heard in humiliation, and evidence encountered in curiosity differs from evidence encountered in terror (\u00a76, pdf-p13).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "INTRODUCES", "object_literal": "Emotional sentience: the felt-evaluative self-regulatory dimension by which life senses how what is happening matters for its continued living \u2014 'life feeling how life is going.'", "fact_text": "The paper defines emotional sentience as the felt-evaluative self-regulatory dimension of life \u2014 the organism's way of sensing not merely what is happening but how it matters for its continued living, development, relation, and action \u2014 characterized as 'life feeling how life is going' (\u00a78, pdf-p14).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "CITES_AUTHOR", "object": "Humberto Maturana", "fact_text": "The paper cites Humberto Maturana for the account of emotions as dynamic bodily dispositions specifying domains of possible action, and for love in Maturana's distinctive biological sense as opening coexistence with the other as a legitimate other (Maturana, 1988; \u00a76, pdf-p13).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "CITES_AUTHOR", "object": "Francisco Varela", "fact_text": "The paper cites Francisco Varela for the foundational accounts of autopoiesis and structural coupling (Maturana & Varela, 1980; Varela et al., 1991; \u00a75, pdf-p12).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "CITES_AUTHOR", "object_literal": "Katherine Peil Kauffman", "fact_text": "The paper attributes the notion of emotional sentience to Katherine Peil Kauffman, rendering it intelligible as the felt-evaluative self-regulatory dimension of life (Kauffman, 2015, 2020; Executive Summary, pdf-p6).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "A patient with depression, trauma, addiction, and chronic pain may be better formulated by process logic (collapsed margin, threat-organized body, narrowed relief, untrustworthy social world) than by stacking four diagnostic boxes; diagnosis remains important but process logic guides repair.", "fact_text": "The paper argues for process logic over diagnostic-box-stacking: a patient with depression, trauma, addiction, and chronic pain may be better formulated by noting that margin has collapsed, the body is organized around threat and exhaustion, relief has narrowed around one behavior, and the social world no longer provides trustworthy recoupling \u2014 diagnosis remains important but the process logic guides the repair plan (\u00a711.13, pdf-p21).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "The framework should be read at four levels of claim: biological-organizational (autopoiesis, structural coupling), embodied extension (valence, emotioning, felt sense), interpretive bridge (emotional sentience without stronger metaphysics), and clinical formulation lens (not a single-cause theory).", "fact_text": "The paper imposes an epistemic discipline guarding against overclaim: the framework should be read at four levels of claim \u2014 autopoiesis/structural coupling as biological-organizational claims; valence/emotioning/felt sense as embodied extensions; emotional sentience as an interpretive bridge requiring no stronger metaphysics; and the clinical application as a formulation lens, not a single-cause theory (\u00a72.1, pdf-p8).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "The social use of autopoiesis requires caution; societies, institutions, and economies are not organisms in the same sense as biological living systems, and coherence-language can become moralizing if misused.", "fact_text": "The paper cautions that the social use of autopoiesis requires care because societies, institutions, and economies are not organisms in the same sense as biological living systems, and that the language of coherence can become moralizing if misused \u2014 lack of coherence should be read as a sign of unmet life conditions, not personal failure (\u00a713, pdf-p25).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "MAKES_CLAIM", "object_literal": "Mental health is not merely the absence of disorder but the capacity for living coherence: to conserve one's organismic integrity, remain viably coupled with a world, feel one's condition truthfully enough to regulate, relate with others as legitimate beings, and participate in shared worlds where life can continue.", "fact_text": "The paper's final claim is that mental health is not merely the absence of disorder but the capacity for living coherence \u2014 to conserve organismic integrity, remain viably coupled with a world, feel one's condition truthfully enough to regulate, relate with others as legitimate beings, and participate in shared worlds where life can continue (\u00a714 Conclusion, pdf-p26).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "ENGAGES_CONCEPT", "object": "life-coherence", "fact_text": "The paper proposes a 'life-coherent psychiatry' \u2014 a clinical orientation that treats neuropsychiatric disease as disturbed living coherence and healing as restoration of viable regulation, relation, feeling, meaning, and options (Glossary, pdf-p27) \u2014 situating it within Sahely's broader life-coherence lineage.", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}, {"subject": "Living Coherence and Neuropsychiatric Disease", "subject_type": "SpecDoc", "predicate": "IN_CLUSTER_WITH", "object": "TOWARDS LIFE-KNOWLEDGE", "fact_text": "Per the About-the-Author note, this clinical white paper is a medical instantiation of Sahely's broader corpus weaving autopoiesis, structural coupling, emotional sentience, life-value onto-axiology, peace theory, and civil-commons thinking, placing it in cluster with the TOWARDS LIFE-KNOWLEDGE umbrella (pdf-p32).", "valid_from": "2026-05-27"}], "group_id": "personal", "create_entities": true}
