docs/research/connections/sahely-life-coherent-discernment-and-repair.md:36:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-16 academic white paper *"Life-Coherent Discernment and Repair: Re-Grounding Spirituality, Religion, Peace, and Geopolitical Conflict in the Protection of Life"* (189 pages — the largest Wave-13 paper; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT GPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely per §1 below). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). This is a **Phase-3** note: it cites the **resolved** post–Bundle-α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and proposes **no admissions**. Every R-claim disposition below is `framing-note-only`. **Single-source rigor:** Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus; cross-post recurrence within his corpus is NOT independent evidence and is not summed as convergence here. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`).
docs/research/connections/sahely-life-coherent-discernment-and-repair.md:91:| R-Cycle | `spore.project-vision` | `rule-in-use` | framing-note-only | C4 9-step repair cycle + C7 11-question stack are operational verb/question stacks at a diagnostic layer adjacent to Spore's operational coordination grammar; cross-layer, not 1:1 mappable. |
docs/research/connections/johar-entangled-intelligence.md:93:This is not an add-on evaluation layer. It is the epistemic coordination grammar through which the field learns.
docs/research/connections/johar-entangled-intelligence.md:99:Johar's manufacturing outsourcing analogy is more immediately legible than the neuroplasticity framing. "Own your context, rent your models" is a one-line principle that communicates the membrane's design rationale to audiences who may not engage with field theory or coordination grammar. It is a translation device, not new content.
docs/research/connections/johar-entangled-intelligence.md:122:This is remarkably close to Spore's foundational claim that coordination grammar — not algorithms, platforms, or models — is the generative layer. Johar arrives at this from institutional design; Spore arrives from agent infrastructure. The convergence is worth noting because it validates the grammar claim from an independent direction: if ontology is infrastructure, then the grammar that structures coordination is the highest-leverage design surface, not the model that generates within it.
tmp/sahely-outreach-draft.md:13:I work on a project called Spore: a small, disciplined "coordination grammar" — a versioned vocabulary for how plural, sovereign communities coordinate without flattening their differences. It's connected to bioregional-commoning work here in Victoria, BC, including commitment-pooling pilots. Over the last few weeks I did a careful intake of your corpus — across the viability-grammar, biology-of-love, civil-commons, and peace papers — mapping each against our canon. It produced over fifty "bridge notes," and, more substantively, six formal decisions where your framework directly changed the canon:
