tmp/wave-9-raw-md/2026-04-10-the-architecture-of-viability-navigating-complex-systems-from-relational.md:4513:Dr. Sahely is the originator of the **Viability Grammar / Viability Geometry** framework, a cross-domain approach that unifies clinical, ecological, and governance systems through the mathematics of relational coherence. His research explores the exceptional algebraic structures underlying complex systems, including the Freudenthal Triple System and the 𝐸7quartic invariant, with the aim of developing a practical calculus for navigating systemic failure and recovery. 
docs/research/connections/sahely-learning-to-read-what-keeps-us-alive.md:46:- **Extraction depth:** the Phase-1 read covered pp 1-5 (cover + TOC) and pp 7-12 (Dedication + Abstract + Keywords + Executive Summary + §0.1-0.2 + §1.1-1.3), producing 12 verbatim C-claims and the Universal-Grammar-of-Viability framework table. Chapters 2-17 + appendices + Children/Students companions (pp 13-97) were **not read** this wave. This bridge note relies on the pp 7-12 substrate; it makes no claims about chapter-internal moves that would require deeper reading.
docs/research/connections/sahely-learning-to-read-what-keeps-us-alive.md:50:The extraction record flags `ai_co_authored: true` with credits `["ChatGPT (GPT-5.2)", "NotebookLM"]`. The 97-page whitepaper is framed (extraction §"Cluster role") as the **general-audience companion** that names *viability illiteracy* as the diagnostic core, written 5 days before the cognitive-scale *Grammar of Viability* companion. Per Phase 1 discipline, the AI tool-credits are surfaced here; this note cites C-claims as Sahely's articulation and does not treat AI-drafting scaffolding as a defeater of attribution. `injection_signal_detected: false` per the extraction record.
