docs/research/connections/sahely-biology-of-living-coordination.md:189:C-13 introduces *wu-wei* as a practical posture of non-forcing participation with the principle "minimum sufficient force required to protect living and open the next coherent movement." This is a NOVEL canonical term in the Sahely corpus, not directly mapped to existing Spore vocabulary. It engages **F5 actuator-logic** (response-doctrine when sensor-evidence disagrees with declared intent) and **F4 representation-authority** (appeal-protocol with proportionate intervention) at the **canon-method** layer — Spore's foundation-docs already specify proportionate response, but do not name a posture-term for the *minimum-sufficient* discipline. Honest-rigor note: *wu-wei* is single-source (Sahely-only at present, with deep historical roots in Daoist tradition but not as articulated for biological-coordination); cluster-counting at Layer-2 DECISION-BRIEF would likely surface ≤1 non-Sahely full cluster within Spore's substrate-relevant traditions (the Daoist tradition itself is rich, but its operational mapping to biological-coordination grammar is Sahely-original).
docs/research/connections/sahely-biology-of-living-coordination.md:207:C-10 (observer-as-distinction-maker) and C-12 domain 5 (observer languaging and distinction-making) engage IC's knowledge-commoning territory and IC's knowledge-integrity discipline at a substrate-resonance layer. IC's 7-intelligence-primitive roster operates at the domain-layer ABOVE Spore's 9-primitive coordination grammar (per ic:ADR-0018 derivation-pointer alignment); Sahely's observer-discipline + Maturana's "objectivity in parentheses" (cited in TOC ch6, not yet extracted) are mature engagements with IC's territory. Descriptive only — no recommendation; cross-stream opt-in is operator-gated.
docs/research/connections/sahely-biology-of-living-coordination.md:215:Not strongly engaged. BKC's territory is commitment-pooling + flow-funding + commons workshop / production-implementation (per cross-repo audit at Ruddick (2026) §7 corrigendum 2026-05-04). Sahely's autopoiesis-enactive substrate is adjacent-but-orthogonal: BKC's commitment-pooling operates at finance / mutual-aid grammar; Sahely's substrate operates at biological-coordination grammar. The two share the "commons-as-verb / commoning-as-practice" frame (`commons-as-verb` slug; Bresnihan / De Angelis) at the abstract layer, but production-implementation doesn't engage Sahely-shape concerns directly.
docs/research/connections/sahely-biology-of-living-coordination.md:338:Per the 3-layer separation discipline (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`): this bridge note is **Layer 1.5 (substrate-grammar map)** carrying DESCRIPTIVE resonance observations. Layer 2 (DECISION-BRIEF cluster-counting) and Layer 3 (ADR ceremony if any) are operator-gated follow-on. No canon-body edits. No commits from this artifact alone. Spore canon at post-Phase-4 plateau preserved: validator 9/30 EXACT held; foundation docs 14; concepts yaml v21; canon-rebuild arc at 34 canon-decisions; no sibling repo writes.
