docs/research/connections/sahely-single-grammar-across-scale.md:40:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-02-09 white paper *"A Single Grammar Across Scale: Invariant Constraints, Viability, and the Emergence of Value from Matter to Civilization"* (63 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.2 + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). This is a **Phase 3 lighter-ceremony** bridge note: it surfaces resonances against the *resolved* post-Bundle-α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; canon-rebuild arc at 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and proposes **no admission**. Every R-claim disposition below is `framing-note-only` (or `decline-with-trigger` for the deliberately-backgrounded sheaf substrate). Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`) — it makes no recommendation for write-side action at IC / bregion / BKC / PM.
