tmp/v2-lens-o-ontology.md:22:Recommended-direction: rescope. Name graph ontology explicitly as the representational layer Spore's tooling supports, *decouple* it from the foundation layer (the claim that coordination is made of things related by edges), and authorise at least one sibling foundation doc that names the coordination grammar in a non-graph ontology (suggested: event/process ontology, since it's closest to Spore's own learning-field workflow where bridge notes *accumulate* over time and selectively promote — which is already event-streamish, not graph-native).
docs/research/connections/sahely-architecture-of-viability.md:59:**Caveat (read first):** This is the Spore-side substrate-grammar map for Bichara Sahely's 2026-04-27 book-length paper *"The Architecture of Viability: A Grammar of Coherence for Life, Mind, Society, and Planet."* The paper is **anchor #3 of Sahely Phase 2** and the **Wave-2 summit paper** — at 531 pages it is the largest single artifact in the entire Sahely corpus and the canonical articulation of the **7-primitive viability grammar `(C, M, X, D, P, R, O)`** (Constraint / Margin / State / Disturbance / Perception / Regulation / Options) that smaller Sahely papers operationalize at specific scales. This note is **descriptive substrate-resonance mapping only**; canon-pressure ASSESSMENT (cluster-counting, admit / decline / scope-condition verdicts) belongs in the Phase 2 DECISION-BRIEF, not here, per the 3-layer separation discipline (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). No write-side recommendations against sibling repos (IC / bregion / BKC / PM) per `feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`. Phase 1 extraction record at `docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-04-27-the-architecture-of-viability-a-grammar-of-coherence-for-life-mind-society-and.md` is the underlying anchor-fidelity evidence; this bridge note cites it and the PDF directly.
