docs/research/connections/sahely-noncommunicable-disease.md:42:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-05-27 white paper *"Noncommunicable Disease and the Worlds We Conserve: A Maturana-Informed Framework for Organism–Niche Coherence, Clinical Care, and Public Health"* (27 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.5 Thinking + NotebookLM, substantive authorship retained by Sahely per §1). It is a **descriptive, framing-note-only** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). **It admits nothing.** The Bundle-α canon-discipline arc (ADRs 0085–0090) is already closed (2026-05-29); this note cites the **resolved** canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; 40 canon-decisions) and maps the post's themes to admitted ADRs/slugs — it does not re-open any DECISION-BRIEF and proposes no new admission. Single-source rigor: Sahely is one AI-co-authored author corpus, and this paper is the domain-applied (clinical/public-health) companion to the 2026-05-21 viability-grammar white paper already bridged at `spore.connection.sahely-maturana-viability-grammar`; cross-post recurrence within the Sahely corpus is **not** independent evidence and is not summed as convergence here. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation.
docs/research/connections/johar-metacognition-stack.md:78:## The Visual Grammar as Architectural Metacognition
docs/research/connections/johar-metacognition-stack.md:80:The **Visual Grammar Atlas** (Shawn Anderson / IndigenomicsAI Dev Sync, April 16) — where the legend emerges from the data model, not patched separately; three coloring modes: ontological, thematic, epistemological — is Layer 10 in action. The Grammar Atlas is not just a UI component — it is an act of architectural metacognition: redesigning the conditions (the grammar) through which the knowledge graph becomes thinkable. The epistemological color mode specifically enacts Layer 4 — making visible the epistemic grammar of each node.
docs/research/connections/johar-metacognition-stack.md:89:6. **Layer 10 → grammar as protocol**: The design of encounter rules, trust weights, and federation protocol IS architectural metacognition.
docs/research/connections/johar-entangled-freedom.md:40:For Spore, this names the developmental condition that makes the grammar viable. Spore's coordination patterns assume relational agents — holons that participate in multiple overlapping wholes. The essay argues this is not merely a design choice but a consequence of what beings actually are. Entangled freedom is the human-developmental ground for Spore's coordination grammar.
docs/research/connections/johar-entangled-freedom.md:65:- **R1**: The Spore lexicon should carry "entangled freedom" as a named design concept: the developmental ground that makes Spore's coordination grammar viable. The entry should include: (a) the refounding of freedom from autonomy-as-separation to participation-within-relation, (b) partial knowing as the condition of relational being — the rationale for why claims must remain revisable and the learning membrane is not a workaround but a structural response, (c) the three recognitions (self as multiplicity, being as co-production, agency as responsibility) as the experiential ground for inhabiting Spore's containment-and-connection architecture, and (d) the distinction from formal sovereignty — Spore already names sovereignty as a constitutional commitment; entangled freedom names the developmental condition that makes sovereignty exercisable. [target: spore.lexicon] [concept: entangled-freedom-and-being] TODO: slug-deferred
tmp/adr-0081-cluster-counting-audit-2026-04-26.md:27:- `docs/research/2026-04-03/compass_artifact_wf-7e2f1acf-184e-4c99-b23e-0abe1177b621_text_markdown.md` §7.2 "Epistemic justice: the deepest challenge" — substantial structural engagement: testimonial injustice (Spore reproduces injustice at infrastructure level via reputation-amplification), hermeneutical injustice (= Gap 9 linguistic-closure-risk; whoever shapes grammar holds hermeneutical power), three concrete intervention proposals (Epistemic Position metadata on every Attestation; Grammar Extension Protocol; periodic Hermeneutic Audits).
docs/research/connections/bennett-every-timeline.md:29:A bridge note on Michael Timothy Bennett's "Every Timeline Is an Opinion" (2026) and its structural relationship to Spore's coordination grammar. Bennett operates at the metaphysical floor — deriving normativity, self-production, and valence from change alone. Spore operates at the coordination layer, giving these dynamics social and technical form.
docs/research/connections/sahely-unifying-grammar-of-viability.md:5:title: "Sahely (2026-02-12) The Unifying Grammar of Viability: Constraint, Memory, and the Preservation of Connected Futures ↔ Spore Coordination-Grammar Substrate"
docs/research/connections/sahely-unifying-grammar-of-viability.md:38:# Sahely (2026-02-12) The Unifying Grammar of Viability: Constraint, Memory, and the Preservation of Connected Futures ↔ Spore Coordination-Grammar Substrate
docs/research/connections/sahely-unifying-grammar-of-viability.md:40:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2026-02-12 book-length synthesis *"The Unifying Grammar of Viability: Constraint, Memory, and the Preservation of Connected Futures"* (118 pages; bsahely.com blog post + companion PDF; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT-5.2 + NotebookLM, with substantive authorship retained by Sahely). It is a **descriptive** Layer-1.5 comparative-intake artifact: it surfaces cross-references between the paper's substrate and Spore's already-resolved post-Bundle-α canon. It is **framing-note-only by default** — it proposes no admission. The Sahely corpus is one AI-co-authored single-author corpus, so cross-post recurrence within it is **not** independent evidence; this note does not claim convergence beyond what one paper supports. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no recommendation for write-side action at IC / bregion / BKC / PM.
docs/research/connections/sahely-unifying-grammar-of-viability.md:121:### 4.1 Four-element grammar ↔ Spore coordination grammar (cross-layer, not 1:1)
docs/research/connections/sahely-unifying-grammar-of-viability.md:158:Sahely's 2026-02-12 book-length synthesis formalizes **viability topology as minimal metaphysics** — a bounded viability set *K*, memory as topological deformation, reachable future space 𝒱(s) as optionality, and a central evaluative maxim (*"preserve the space in which the future remains possible"*). Its four-element grammar (Constraint / Memory / Control / Value) sits at the metaphysical layer, adjacent-but-cross-layer to Spore's operational coordination grammar.
tmp/johar-power-framework-synthesis-2026-04-22.md:113:- **Layer 1 (authority-over-rule-levels)** aligns with enumerated-powers-by-role and "smallest viable locus" thinking. The three-level stratification mirrors loop-fluency: feel (operational), narrate (collective-choice), respond-and-learn (constitutional). **Confirmed.**
tmp/johar-power-framework-synthesis-2026-04-22.md:129:ADR-0047's three layers are all **structural givens**. Layer 1 says who *can* set rules; Layer 2 says binding is asymmetric; Layer 3 says membrane-authorize is asymmetric. These are **pre-settable.**
tmp/v2-lens-w-wider.md:5:Reading the wider corpus reveals three patterns v1 did not fully weight. First, the canon is not one canon — it is **three canons layered over each other**: (a) an aspirational coordination grammar (the original vision/foundation docs v1 audited), (b) a P2P-wiki-derived commons-critical doctrine layer (ADR-0002/3/4/5 and the accompanying framing notes), and (c) a meta-corpus governance stack (ADR-0011/12/21/22/24/25 and the review protocols). v1 audited layer (a) almost in isolation, but layer (b) has silently rewritten what the foundation docs *mean* through "motivating-language additions" — enough that several v1 criticisms are already contested in-corpus without v1 noticing. Second, the corpus contains **at least six load-bearing concepts missing from v1's list of 13**: reproductive labor / commons-as-verb, boundary-commoning, the three-layer coordination stack, polycentric-governance-vs-decentralization, openwashing discipline, and structural-coupling/autopoietic-closure as the unnamed theory of "membrane." Third, the corpus is much more honest about several of v1's findings than v1 assumes — the canon already calls bioregion "holon-in-formation" (ADR-0038), already demotes Friston/Bennett (ADR-0039), already tiers the graph projections (ADR-0036) — v1 audited a pre-R4 draft in places where post-R4 canon already addresses the issue.
