docs/research/connections/sahely-rationality-after-collapse.md:44:**Caveat (read first):** This is a Spore-side substrate-resonance bridge note for Bichara Sahely's 2025-12-28 white paper *"Rationality After Collapse: Upgrading Game Theory for Life in a Finite World"* (23 pages; subtitle *A Life-Value Coherent Framework for Decision-Making across Pandemic, Climate, and AI Systems*; AI-co-authored with ChatGPT5.2 + NotebookLM). It is a **descriptive** comparative-intake artifact at Layer 1.5 of the intake-to-vocab-admission program (`feedback_intake_to_vocab_admission_program.md`). This is a **Phase 3 framing-note-only** note: it cites the **resolved** post-Bundle-α canon state (concepts-yaml v24; 4 cross-cutting doctrines; canon-rebuild arc at 40 canon-decisions through ADR-0090) and surfaces NO admission proposals. The Sahely corpus's substantive life-value / trap-shape / civil-commons / care / margin / perception canon-pressure was already adjudicated and admitted across Bundle α (ADRs 0085–0090); this note maps the post against that resolved state. Cross-repo §5 is descriptive comparison only per stream-scope discipline (`feedback_workstream_scope_discipline.md`); it makes no write-side recommendation for IC/bregion/BKC/PM.
docs/research/connections/sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md:75:This is a **cross-corpus synthesis bridge note**, not a canon-pressure document. It does not shift canon state, admit slugs, or trigger ADRs. It maps Sahely's six-layer mathematical-substrate derivation chain (from *From Entanglement to Governance: The Geometry of Coherence Across Scales*, 2026-04-02) against the existing Spore sheaf research substrate (8 prior bridge notes + 1 synthesis + the live sheaf-explorer pedagogy at [sheaf.lol](https://sheaf.lol)) and against operator's recent operational-engineering bridges (JANUS / SHEAF-CAPABILITIES / Zhao 2025). Substrate-resonance descriptive map; design-discipline distillation; cross-corpus KG-triple authoring surface.
