docs/research/connections/sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md:323:This is Sahely's load-bearing thesis — and it composes deeply with Spore's project-vision Core Thesis (coordination grammar over system substrate). The framing "viability is coherence of relations" sits at the *epistemic-paradigm* layer rather than the mathematical-substrate layer; it is the philosophical commitment that organizes Sahely's six-layer mathematical machinery.
docs/research/connections/sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md:325:Spore canon's `coordination-grammar-over-system-substrate` stance (per project-vision Core Thesis) is the closest analog. Where Spore says *"grammar of how coordination works"*, Sahely says *"geometry of relational coherence"*. The frames are compositionally compatible — Spore's operational coordination grammar maps cleanly onto Sahely's relational-coherence geometric framing — but they are not identical.
docs/research/connections/sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md:374:- **Bodnar et al. 2022** *Neural Sheaf Diffusion* (cited in `sheaf-theory-formalization`): NSD as graph-learning architecture; covered in sheaf.lol §10c interactive Neural Diffusion card.
docs/research/connections/sheaf-substrate-multi-source-synthesis.md:376:- **Zhao et al. 2025** *Asynchronous Nonlinear Sheaf Diffusion* (per `zhao-async-nonlinear-sheaf-diffusion`): formal convergence theorem under partial-asynchrony (Theorem `thm:linear_conv`); periodic linear convergence every B+1 iterations; rate ∝ λ₂(L_F). Already shipped in sheaf.lol §8 sync/async demo + §9 Research Frontier card (per Zhao bridge note §Process Notes).
