docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-03-17-viability-geometry-a-minimal-relational-framework-for-persistence-in-complex.md:84:> "Section 7: Triadic Closure in Adaptive Systems — 7.1 Positional Geometry: Constraints, Margins, and State + 7.2 Disturbance Response: State, Disturbance, and Regulation + 7.3 Early Warning: Margins, Disturbance, and Perception + 7.4 Governance of Constraints: Constraints, Perception, and Regulation + 7.5 Preservation of Adaptive Capacity: Margins, Optionality, and Regulation + 7.6 Environmental Compression: Constraints, Disturbance, and Optionality + 7.7 Navigating Possible Futures: State, Perception, and Optionality. Section 8: The Canonical Viability Triads and the Fano Grammar — 8.1 Steiner Triple Systems + 8.2 The Fano Representation of the Viability Grammar + 8.3 Structural Implications + 8.4 Why Seven Roles Are Necessary + 8.5 From Combinatorics to Geometry"
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-03-17-viability-geometry-a-minimal-relational-framework-for-persistence-in-complex.md:87:> "Section 9: The Geometry of Survival: The Viability Manifold — Constraint Boundaries and Viable Regions + Margins as Distance to Failure + Optionality and the Cone of Viable Futures + Disturbance and Regulatory Dynamics + Collapse as a Geometric Phenomenon + From Relational Grammar to Dynamical Systems. Section 13: Civilizational Viability and the Life-Ground — Planetary Constraints + Disturbances in Civilizational Systems + Margin Erosion at the Planetary Scale + Optionality in Civilizational Systems + Geopolitical Conflict as Viability Risk + Structural Violence and Systemic Fragility + Civilizational Trajectories."
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-03-17-viability-geometry-a-minimal-relational-framework-for-persistence-in-complex.md:124:**Very High.** This is the MATHEMATICAL ANCHOR of Wave 5 — formalizes the viability-grammar that Trilogy papers articulate phenomenologically. 15 high-fidelity claims captured; the §5-§6 partition + §7-§8 Fano grammar + §9 Viability Manifold + §13 Civilizational application + Appendices C/D (octonion + E_7 speculative connections) are load-bearing. **Targeted second pass through §1 Viability Question (motivation), §2-§4 three Case Studies (medicine + ecology + finance cross-domain unification), §7 7 canonical triads with names (Positional Geometry / Disturbance Response / Early Warning / Governance of Constraints / Preservation of Adaptive Capacity / Environmental Compression / Navigating Possible Futures), §8 Fano Grammar formalization, §9 Viability Manifold geometric formalization, §10 Structural Sources of Fragility, §11 Viability Functional and Relational Coherence, §12 Implications for Design and Governance, §13 Civilizational Viability scale application, Appendix A (Constraint Geometry formalization), Appendix B (Steiner Triple System), Appendix C (Octonions), Appendix D (Freudenthal + E_7), Appendix F (Empirical Indicators)** would yield ~40-50 additional substrate claims with formal-mathematical anchoring. **Wave-5 anchor candidate alongside Trilogy capstone #5; sister-anchor pair with Wave-1 sheaf-geometry-cluster Entanglement-to-Governance**.
