docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-02-28-money-scarcity-and-violence-monetary-architecture-institutional-design-and.md:28:**Cluster role**: Wave-7 same-day-pair with #7 (Life First / Viability Budgeting). Pairs as the **civilizational-theoretical** complement to #7's **practitioner-policy** framework. Where #7 names a specific framework (Viability Budgeting) and gives implementation pathways, #8 grounds the architecture-vs-money-as-villain distinction in deeper civilizational analysis: real-vs-institutional-constraints / four-principle architecture / transition considerations / civilizational implication. Substrate-continuity with anchor #6 (Grammar of Violence) — applies the violence-architecture diagnosis specifically to monetary systems' role in producing structural violence.
docs/research/corpus-review/originals/sahely-extractions/2026-04-10-the-architecture-of-viability-navigating-complex-systems-from-relational.md:33:**Cluster role**: **WAVE-9 ANCHOR**. Mathematical-formalization capstone of the 4-post iteration arc (#1→#2→#3→#4). Lifts the relational grammar (intuited in #1, multi-agent in #2, perception-value in #3, navigation-stack in #4) into a **mathematically explicit framework**: seven irreducible primitives → Fano plane geometry → octonion algebra → 27-dimensional Albert algebra → 56-dimensional Freudenthal Triple System → E7 quartic invariant. This is the **earlier framing** of the doctrine Sahely later expanded to the 531pp summit (Wave-2 anchor #6, published April 27, titled "The Architecture of Viability: A Grammar of Coherence for Life, Mind, Society, and Cosmos"). **EXTENDS edge → Wave-2 anchor #6** confirmed via direct comparison: shared "Architecture of Viability" title + shared seven-primitive substrate + shared E7 invariant; Wave-2 #6 is the 4×-expansion extending to cosmos / life / mind / society scope.
